        reason: 'Working at the Rockefeller Institute\'s Princeton laboratories, Stanley purified juice from mosaic-diseased tobacco plants and obtained needle-like crystals that, when redissolved, still infected healthy plants. His paper "Isolation of a crystalline protein possessing the properties of tobacco-mosaic virus" appeared in Science on 28 June 1935, recording for the first time that a virus could be reduced to a crystalline form that preserved its biological activity.',
