        reason: 'Loewi performed his two-frog-heart perfusion experiment in 1921 and published it that year as "Über humorale Übertragbarkeit der Herznervenwirkung" in Pflügers Archiv für die gesamte Physiologie. The transfer of inhibitory effect via fluid alone recorded the first direct evidence that a nerve acts by releasing a chemical messenger ("Vagusstoff"), against the then-dominant view that synaptic transmission was electrical.',
