        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Pauling, Itano, Singer and Wells used moving-boundary electrophoresis to compare haemoglobin from normal individuals and from sickle-cell patients, finding that sickle haemoglobin (HbS) carries a more positive charge. Their paper in Science recorded the first evidence that a disease originates in a defined abnormality of a single protein molecule, introducing the term "molecular disease."',
