        reason: 'Louis XVI appointed a commission drawn from the Académie royale des sciences and the Faculty of Medicine to test the claims empirically. The commissioners (Franklin, Lavoisier, Bailly, Guillotin and others) ran controlled trials — magnetising objects without the subject\'s knowledge, and convincing subjects they were being magnetised when they were not — and found that reactions tracked belief rather than any physical agent. Their report, signed 11 August 1784, concluded that no magnetic fluid existed and that imagination alone produced the observed effects, formally overturning Mesmer\'s physical claim.',
