        reason: 'After the theological consultors of the Holy Office assessed (24 February 1616) that the heliocentric propositions were "formally heretical" and at least erroneous in faith, the Congregation of the Index issued its decree on 5 March 1616. It branded the Pythagorean (Copernican) doctrine of a moving Earth and a central, immobile Sun as false and contrary to Scripture, banned outright works that defended it as physical truth, and suspended Copernicus\'s De revolutionibus until passages could be amended — fixing the Church\'s official position against heliocentrism for the next two centuries.',
