        reason: 'After Leibniz appealed to the Royal Society for a fair hearing on accusations of plagiarism, the Society in April 1712 passed a resolution affirming Newton\'s precedence, based on a committee of Newton\'s supporters that contained no Continental mathematician, never solicited Leibniz\'s testimony, and whose report Newton himself composed. The committee\'s finding was issued in 1713 as the Commercium Epistolicum, concluding that Newton was the first inventor and that Leibniz had taken his calculus from letters communicating Newton\'s ideas.',
