        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '1277-03-18',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'During a visitation of the University of Oxford, Archbishop Robert Kilwardby prohibited the teaching of thirty articles — sixteen in grammar and logic and the remainder in natural philosophy — under threat of academic penalty. The list, recorded in the university\'s documents and reproduced in the surviving registers, included the thesis that there is only one substantial form in a composite being (the unicity of form), which bore on Aquinas\'s account of the human soul and body. The condemnation is a contemporaneous institutional act, issued just eleven days after the parallel Paris condemnation of 7 March 1277.',
