        reason: 'Kilwardby\'s successor as Archbishop of Canterbury, the Franciscan John Pecham, renewed and reinforced the Oxford condemnation in 1284, keeping the unicity-of-form thesis under censure in England. Yet the doctrine it targeted came to prevail within Thomism, and after Aquinas was canonized in 1323 the Paris articles touching his teaching were formally revoked in 1325; the standing of the 1277 Oxford censure as against Aquinas thus became contested rather than a settled verdict, a question debated by historians of scholasticism ever since.',
