        reason: 'After Marsilius and John of Jandun fled to the court of the excommunicated emperor Louis IV of Bavaria, John XXII moved against the Defensor Pacis. On 23 October 1327 a commission of theologians at Avignon condemned five propositions excerpted from the work — including the denials of Christ\'s payment of tribute as obligatory, of papal plenitude of power, and of the clergy\'s coercive jurisdiction — as false, contrary to Holy Scripture, and heretical; the bull Licet iuxta doctrinam declared the two authors manifest heretics. The condemnation survives as a contemporaneous papal act.',
