        reason: 'Working at the Buyid court of Adud al-Dawla in Isfahan, al-Sufi compiled the Kitab suwar al-kawakib (964), a revised catalogue of Ptolemy\'s constellations corrected against his own observations and Arab star lore. Among the stars of Andromeda he noted a faint "little cloud" — the patch now identified as the Andromeda Galaxy (M31) — making his treatise the earliest surviving record of a galaxy beyond our own. The work survives in numerous illustrated manuscript copies, several within a century or two of the original.',
