        reason: 'Rival recensions and copyists\' errors had left the wording of the classics in dispute, and corrupt readings were being introduced to support particular interpretations. Cai Yong and other scholars petitioned the throne to fix the text; the Hou Hanshu records that in spring, the third month of Xiping 4, an edict "ordered the scholars to correct the text of the Five Classics and carve them on stone, set up outside the gate of the Imperial Academy." The decision to establish an official standard edition was thereby placed on the record.',
