        reason: 'The carving, supervised by Cai Yong, was completed in 183 CE: 46 stelae of some seven classics stood at the Taixue, and the Hou Hanshu reports that scholars and students thronged to copy and collate against them, with carriages crowding the streets daily. The stones served as the first state-authorised master copy of the canon, and the principle of an imperially fixed standard text became established — repeated in later dynasties\' own stone classics. Modern scholarship dates the project securely to the Xiping era (175–183 CE) and counts surviving fragments in museum collections.',
