    text: 'Pappus of Alexandria, in his commentary on Ptolemy\'s Almagest, worked through the place and time of the solar eclipse at Alexandria of 18 October 320 CE — writing as if of an eclipse he had recently seen — a dated application of Ptolemaic parallax-based eclipse prediction that fixes his floruit to about 320 CE.',
