    externalId: 'trajectory:mawangdui-tomb3-sealed-168bce',
    text: 'The silk manuscripts sealed in Tomb 3 at Mawangdui (Changsha) — buried with Li Xi, son of the Marquis of Dai, in the second lunar month of the twelfth year of Emperor Wen of Han (168 BCE), the burial dated by the tomb\'s own inventory tablet — include the Wushi\'er Bingfang (Recipes for Fifty-Two Ailments) and companion texts that are the oldest surviving Chinese medical manuscripts, together with astronomical silks recording planetary periods and forms of comets.',
