    text: 'On 9 October 1963 a landslide of some 260 million cubic metres broke off Monte Toc into the reservoir of the Vajont Dam in northern Italy, throwing a wave over the dam crest that obliterated Longarone and neighbouring villages and killed about 1,900 people; the slope\'s instability had been known and warned of during construction, and Italian courts later found the disaster foreseeable.',
