        reason: 'After Israel attacked Egypt on 29 October 1956 and Anglo-French forces intervened, suspicions of prior collusion circulated immediately, but the three governments concealed the Sèvres meeting; Eden ordered the British copy of the protocol destroyed and on 20 December 1956 told the House of Commons there had been "no foreknowledge that Israel would attack Egypt." With leaks alleging collusion but no documentary proof, the existence of a secret pact was contested rather than established.',
