        reason: 'At about 12:37 on 10 July 1976 a runaway reaction in a reactor producing trichlorophenol at the ICMESA plant (a Givaudan/Hoffmann-La Roche subsidiary) burst a safety disc and vented an aerosol cloud over Meda, Seveso and neighbouring communes. Residents soon reported burns and sickened animals, but the identity and danger of the released material were not communicated, leaving the nature of the contamination genuinely unknown to the public and local authorities.',
