        reason: 'Pursuing Xiongnu raiders into Shanxi in the cold of winter, Emperor Gaozu pressed ahead of his infantry with his cavalry and was drawn in by Modu, who concealed his best troops and showed only weak detachments. On Mount Baideng the Han vanguard was cut off and besieged for seven days, the soldiers suffering frostbite that cost many of them their fingers; the emperor reached terms — by tradition through a bribe carried to Modu\'s consort by the adviser Chen Ping — and was allowed to slip out. The encirclement of the dynasty\'s founder and his narrow escape were set down in the Han court\'s historical record.',
