    text: 'The millenarian Way of Great Peace led by Zhang Jue had set a coordinated rising across the Han empire for the jiazi day of the third month of 184 CE under the slogan "The Azure Heaven is dead; the Yellow Heaven shall stand; the year is jiazi, and the realm shall greatly prosper"; but when the disciple Tang Zhou betrayed the conspiracy to the court and the agent Ma Yuanyi was arrested and executed at Luoyang, Zhang Jue launched the Yellow Turban Rebellion early — conventionally 4 March 184 — his followers binding yellow scarves on their heads and rising in eight provinces at once, the great revolt that broke the authority of the Eastern Han.',
