        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '0184-03-04',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The Book of Later Han records that Zhang Jue had organized hundreds of thousands of followers into thirty-six commands and planned a simultaneous rising for the jiazi day of the third month, the agent Ma Yuanyi coordinating sympathizers inside the capital; when the disciple Tang Zhou denounced the plot, Ma Yuanyi was seized and torn apart at Luoyang and a purge began, so Zhang Jue sent word for his followers to rise at once. The betrayal, the execution, and the premature outbreak are entered in the chronicle of the Eastern Han.',
