        reason: 'The stele\'s own inscription records that the king, who had died in the renzi year (412), was moved to his tumulus on the 29th day (yuryu) of the ninth month of the jiayin year (414), at which time the monument was raised. The text — composed at the Goguryeo court and carved into a single granite shaft near the capital at Gungnae (modern Ji\'an) — is a contemporaneous primary record of the burial and of the reign\'s major campaigns.',
