        reason: 'Ptolemy, in Almagest III.1, reports that "those around Aristarchus" observed the summer solstice in the 50th year of the first Callippic period — equivalent to 280 BCE. Hipparchus took this dated solstice as a fixed earlier point: comparing it with his own solstice observation 145 years later, he found the interval fell short of an exact number of whole days by a small fraction, and from that discrepancy derived his corrected estimate that the tropical year is about 1/300 of a day shorter than 365¼ days.',
