        reason: 'Mercury, never far from the Sun and the most awkward planet to observe, received in the Almagest a model whose apsidal line and eccentricity rested on these dated elongations; the construction was carried forward by Islamic and Latin astronomers for centuries. The elongation dates are confirmable by modern retrocalculation, and 1/2 February 141 CE is independently recognised as the endpoint of Ptolemy\'s own observational record.',
