        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The presence of an American crop deep in pre-contact Polynesia — carbonised sweet potato from the Cook Islands radiocarbon-dated to AD 1210–1400, and a *kumara*/*kumar* word shared between Polynesian and Andean Quechua — long pointed to prehistoric contact across the eastern Pacific. Caroline Roullier and colleagues, sequencing chloroplast and nuclear markers from historical herbarium collections gathered before modern plant movements blurred the picture, report in PNAS a distinct "Kumara" lineage in eastern Polynesia tracing to the Peru–Ecuador region, supporting a single pre-Columbian human-mediated introduction consistent with a Polynesian voyage to South America and back.',
