        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1128-12-08',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'John of Worcester, continuing the chronicle of Florence of Worcester, entered under Saturday 8 December 1128 that from morning to evening two black spots appeared on the disc of the Sun, one in the upper part and the larger in the lower, and he added a coloured illustration showing the two spots on the solar disc. The dated entry and its drawing are preserved in the autograph manuscript (CCC MS 157) and constitute the earliest known graphical record of sunspots.',
