        reason: 'Willis and Stephenson (Annales Geophysicae, 2001) establish the date of the Worcester observation as firmly fixed at AD 1128 December 8 and show that the red auroral display recorded from Songdo, Korea, on the night of 13 December 1128 — about five days later — matches the typical delay between a large sunspot group crossing the central solar disc and a low-latitude aurora, confirming an intense recurrent geomagnetic storm and the authenticity of the medieval sunspot record.',
