        reason: 'Of the historical Galactic supernovae of the last millennium, SN 1181 alone lacks an unambiguous remnant. Stephenson and Green\'s catalogue of historical supernovae notes that the pulsar/remnant 3C 58 had been proposed as the relic of the 1181 event, but its inferred age and expansion sit uneasily with a 1181 origin, leaving the identification unresolved for centuries.',
