        occurredAt: '1532-11-16',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Atahualpa, fresh from victory in the Inca civil war, agreed to meet the Spaniards at Cajamarca. When he entered the square borne on his litter, the friar Vicente de Valverde presented the Requerimiento and a breviary; Pizarro then sprang the ambush, his cavalry and arquebusiers cutting down the emperor\'s attendants and taking Atahualpa prisoner. Pizarro\'s secretary Francisco de Xerez, an eyewitness, recorded the date and the seizure in his Verdadera relación de la conquista del Perú, published at Seville in 1534.',
