        reason: 'Multiple independent accounts converge on the event: the eyewitness narratives of Xerez, Miguel de Estete and Pedro Pizarro from the Spanish side, and Andean testimony gathered later by Juan de Betanzos (who interviewed Inca who had been present) and Titu Cusi Yupanqui. John Hemming\'s The Conquest of the Incas (1970) synthesises these sources into the standard modern account; the date, location and fact of the capture are settled, with scholarship debating its causes and demography rather than its occurrence.',
