    text: 'On 27 December 1512 the Spanish crown promulgated the Laws of Burgos, the first codified body of law governing Spanish conduct toward the Indigenous peoples of the Americas — a code of thirty-five ordinances regulating the encomienda on Hispaniola, requiring Christian instruction, limiting forced labour, and prohibiting the worst physical abuses of the Taíno.',
