        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1644-06-11',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'In a letter to his fellow mathematician Michelangelo Ricci dated 11 June 1644, Torricelli reported the inverted mercury-tube experiment (carried out with the help of Vincenzo Viviani) and drew the two radical conclusions that the column is held up by the weight of the surrounding air and that the space left at the top of the tube is genuinely empty. The letter contains his celebrated remark that "we live submerged at the bottom of an ocean of the element air, which by unquestioned experiments is known to have weight." It was the first instrument to measure atmospheric pressure.',
