        reason: 'Torricelli\'s interpretation was confirmed and generalised when Blaise Pascal\'s Puy de Dôme experiment of 19 September 1648 showed the mercury column falling with altitude, and was further reinforced by Otto von Guericke\'s air-pump demonstrations and Robert Boyle\'s pneumatics. The existence of the vacuum and the reality of atmospheric pressure became settled physics; the unit "torr" commemorates the experiment.',
