        reason: 'A peaceful procession of tens of thousands of workers and their families, organised by the Assembly of Russian Factory and Mill Workers under the priest Georgy Gapon, converged on the Winter Palace carrying icons, portraits of the Tsar, and a petition for an eight-hour day, fair wages, and political reform. Cordons of Imperial Guard infantry and Cossacks opened fire at the Narva Gate, on Nevsky Prospekt, and before the palace; official figures admitted about 96 dead and several hundred wounded, while opposition estimates ran far higher. The shooting in the capital was reported immediately in the Russian and foreign press.',
