    externalId: 'trajectory:douglass-hh39-tree-ring-bridge-1929',
    text: 'On 22 June 1929 the astronomer Andrew E. Douglass cross-dated beam HH-39, recovered from the Whipple Ruin at Show Low, Arizona, against his floating prehistoric tree-ring sequence — bridging the gap to the living-tree chronology and producing a continuous record reaching back to about 700 CE that, for the first time, fixed absolute calendar dates to the Ancestral Puebloan ruins of the American Southwest.',
