        toAxis: 'SETTLED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1929-12-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'Douglass reported the breakthrough in the December 1929 National Geographic Magazine ("The Secret of the Southwest Solved by Talkative Tree Rings"), publishing absolute construction dates for major ruins including Pueblo Bonito. Dendrochronology became an established absolute-dating method in archaeology, independent of and predating radiocarbon dating, and the tree-ring dates for Southwestern sites are settled.',
