    text: 'At the First Palenque Round Table (Primera Mesa Redonda de Palenque), held 14–22 December 1973 and organised by Merle Greene Robertson, Linda Schele, Peter Mathews and Floyd Lounsbury worked out the dynastic succession of Palenque from its own inscriptions in a single afternoon — reading the name of the king Pakal and several of his successors, the first reconstruction of a Classic Maya royal line and a decisive demonstration that Maya inscriptions record real dynastic history.',
