        occurredAt: '1973-12-14',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'At a working conference on the art, iconography and dynastic history of Palenque convened by Merle Greene Robertson on 14–22 December 1973, Schele, Mathews and Lounsbury combined Tatiana Proskouriakoff\'s historical reading of the inscriptions with Yuri Knorozov\'s phonetic approach to read the personal names and accession dates of a sequence of Palenque rulers, identifying the king buried in the Temple of the Inscriptions as Pakal. Their joint paper "Lords of Palenque: The Glyphic Evidence" was presented at the meeting and published in its 1974 proceedings, recording the reconstruction of the dynasty.',
