    text: 'The Grolier Codex — a fragmentary Maya screenfold book reportedly looted from a cave in Chiapas — was first shown to the public at the Grolier Club in New York on 20 April 1971; long suspected of being a modern forgery, its authenticity was contested for over four decades before scientific study led Mexico\'s INAH to declare it genuine in 2018, making it the oldest surviving book of the Americas.',
