        reason: 'A 2015 reassessment by Coe, Houston, Miller and Taube concluded the codex was authentic, and in 2018 Mexico\'s Instituto Nacional de Antropología e Historia, after a battery of physical and chemical analyses, formally declared the manuscript genuine and dated it to roughly 1021–1154 CE — the oldest surviving codex of the Americas. The decades-long forgery dispute is now resolved in favour of authenticity, and the book was renamed the Maya Codex of Mexico.',
