        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Commissioned by the Institute for Government Research (later the Brookings Institution) and funded by the Rockefeller Foundation, a survey team under technical director Lewis Meriam spends seven months visiting reservations, agencies, and boarding schools. Their 847-page report, submitted to Interior Secretary Hubert Work on 21 February 1928, documents that "the income of the typical Indian family is low and the earned income extremely low," that Indian health is "bad," and that the allotment of communal land under the Dawes Act of 1887 had impoverished rather than assimilated Native Americans. The report is a contemporaneous, evidence-based record of conditions on the reservations.',
