        reason: 'The Report\'s findings became the documentary foundation of "Indian New Deal" reform: new allotments fell sharply, boarding-school policy was revised, and within six years the Indian Reorganization Act of 18 June 1934 formally ended the allotment policy the Report had condemned. The Meriam Report is settled in the historiography of federal Indian policy as the watershed indictment of allotment and assimilation that precipitated the reforms of the 1930s.',
