        reason: 'Drafted under Commissioner of Indian Affairs John Collier and shaped by the Meriam Report\'s indictment of allotment, the Act halts further allotment of tribal land, extends the trust status of existing Indian lands indefinitely, restores "surplus" lands to tribes, and lets tribes organise governments and business corporations. President Roosevelt signs it as the Act of 18 June 1934, 48 Stat. 984. It reverses the policy of the Dawes Act of 1887, which had cut tribal landholdings from about 138 million acres to roughly 48 million.',
