        reason: 'Although the assimilationist "termination" policy of the 1950s sought to undo parts of Collier\'s reforms, the Indian Reorganization Act was never repealed: its end to allotment was permanent, more than two million acres were restored to tribal trust within twenty years, and the tribal constitutions and corporations it authorised remain the legal foundation of many tribal governments today. The Act\'s date, content, and reversal of allotment are settled history.',
