        reason: 'During fieldwork at the Tugriken Shire locality of the Djadokhta Formation, members of the joint Polish–Mongolian expedition — among them Teresa Maryańska, Altangerel Perle, and colleagues — uncovered the intertwined skeletons of a Velociraptor and a Protoceratops, the predator\'s sickle-clawed hind foot embedded at the herbivore\'s throat and its forelimb gripped in the Protoceratops\' beak. The find, recovered on 3 August 1971, was documented by the expedition and published in the palaeontological literature.',
