        occurredAt: '1804-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Two months after the French defeat at Vertières, the generals of the former colony of Saint-Domingue gather at Gonaïves and have Dessalines proclaimed general-in-chief; the Declaration, drafted by his secretary Louis Boisrond-Tonnerre, renounces France forever and restores the Indigenous name Haiti. The act is printed at once on the government press and disseminated, ending the world\'s only successful large-scale slave revolt with the creation of a new sovereign state.',
