        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2010-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'For more than two centuries no original printed copy of the Declaration was known to exist in Haiti, the text surviving only through later transcriptions. In 2010 Julia Gaffield, a Duke University graduate student, located an original government-printed copy in the UK National Archives at Kew — followed by a second in 2011 — confirming the authoritative text and date of the founding document and settling its provenance in the historical record.',
