        fromAxis: 'RECORDED',
        toAxis: 'SETTLED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1772-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'Chappe\'s observations were carried back to France and published posthumously as "Voyage en Californie pour l\'observation du passage de Vénus" (1772), edited by Cassini de Thury. Combined with the other 1769 transit observations from Tahiti, Hudson Bay and northern Europe, the Baja California data fed the computation of the solar parallax and the astronomical unit to within a few percent of the modern value — settling Chappe\'s station as one of the contributing observations of the eighteenth-century parallax campaign.',
