        reason: 'Under sustained British naval pressure — culminating in the 1845 Aberdeen Act that authorized the Royal Navy to seize Brazilian slave ships — the government of Emperor Pedro II, with Justice Minister Eusébio de Queirós Coutinho Matoso da Câmara, pushes Law No. 581 through the General Assembly. The statute prohibits the importation of enslaved Africans, classes the traffic as piracy, and provides for the seizure and adjudication of slaving vessels. The promulgated law is the contemporaneous primary record.',
