        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1881-06-02',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Challenged publicly by the veterinary press to prove his attenuated anthrax vaccine, Pasteur — with Émile Roux and Charles Chamberland — vaccinated half of a herd of sheep, goats, and cattle on 5 and 17 May 1881, then on 31 May injected the entire herd with a virulent anthrax culture. When observers gathered at the farm of Pouilly-le-Fort near Melun on 2 June 1881, every vaccinated animal was healthy and every unvaccinated control was dead or dying. The dramatic, witnessed result was reported in the press and to the Académie des sciences.',
