    text: 'On 6 July 1885 Louis Pasteur administered his experimental post-exposure rabies vaccine to nine-year-old Joseph Meister, who had been badly mauled by a rabid dog; the boy never developed rabies — the first human use of the rabies vaccine and a founding success of immunization against a viral disease.',
