        reason: 'The act of founding the mosque was recorded at the time on coral-stone panels in floriated Kufic script set into the qibla wall beside the mihrab. The inscription names the patron, the sheikh Abu ʿImran Musa ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, and dates the construction to the month of Dhu al-Qaʿda 500 AH (corresponding to 1107 CE). It is a contemporaneous, internally dated primary record of an established Muslim community on the Swahili coast in the early twelfth century.',
