        occurredAt: '1922-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'The inscription was published and read by Samuel Flury ("The Kufic Inscriptions of Kisimkazi Mosque," 1922) and discussed in the standard surveys of the East African coast by G.S.P. Freeman-Grenville and others. The 1107 date is accepted as the earliest securely dated inscription on the Swahili coast and as evidence for an organized Islamic community on Zanzibar by the early twelfth century, though most of the present fabric of the mosque is a later rebuilding around the original inscribed panels.',
