    externalId: 'trajectory:john-worcester-sunspot-1128',
    text: 'On 8 December 1128 the English monk John of Worcester observed and drew two large dark spots crossing the disc of the Sun — the earliest known dated drawing of sunspots — and a brilliant aurora was recorded in Korea five days later, on 13 December 1128.',
