        reason: 'Pursuing Patrick Manson\'s hypothesis that mosquitoes transmit malaria, Ross fed "dappled-winged" mosquitoes on the blood of a patient named Husein Khan and dissected them over successive days. On 20 August 1897 — later commemorated as World Mosquito Day — he saw pigmented cells (oocysts) growing in the insect\'s stomach wall, the parasite\'s development outside the human host. He recorded the finding in his notebook and published it in the Indian Medical Gazette on 27 August 1897 and the British Medical Journal in December 1897.',
