    text: 'Johannes Diderik van der Waals, in his doctoral dissertation "Over de Continuïteit van den Gas- en Vloeistoftoestand" (On the Continuity of the Gaseous and Liquid States) defended at Leiden on 14 June 1873, derived an equation of state for real gases that accounts for the finite size of molecules and the attractive forces between them — unifying the gaseous and liquid states and explaining the critical point.',
