        reason: 'Defending his thesis at Leiden University on 14 June 1873, van der Waals modified the ideal-gas law into (P + a/V²)(V − b) = RT, where the constant b corrects for the non-zero volume of molecules and a for their mutual attraction. Treating a fluid as molecules of finite size with intermolecular forces, the equation explains the continuous transition between gas and liquid and predicts a critical temperature above which no amount of pressure liquefies the gas — the first successful molecular theory of the liquid–gas transition.',
