        reason: 'At the Physikalisch-Technische Reichsanstalt in Berlin, Meissner and Ochsenfeld measured the magnetic field distribution outside superconducting tin and lead samples cooled in an applied field. They found that on crossing the transition temperature the metal cancelled nearly all of its interior field — the flux was expelled, not merely frozen in. The result, "Ein neuer Effekt bei Eintritt der Supraleitfähigkeit," appeared in Die Naturwissenschaften, vol. 21, pp. 787–788. This contradicted the expectation from treating a superconductor as merely a perfect conductor, for which a pre-existing interior field would have been trapped.',
