        toAxis: 'SETTLED',
        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '1942-10-09',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The Statute took immediate effect for Canada, South Africa, and the Irish Free State; Australia, New Zealand, and Newfoundland had to formally adopt its provisions for them to apply. Australia adopted the Statute by the Statute of Westminster Adoption Act 1942 (assented 9 October 1942, backdated to 3 September 1939); New Zealand adopted it in 1947. The principle that the Dominions were sovereign legislatures, the UK Parliament unable to bind them without consent, became the settled constitutional foundation of the Commonwealth.',
