    text: 'On 15 March 1937 Bernard Fantus opened the first hospital blood bank in the United States at Cook County Hospital in Chicago — a laboratory for collecting, typing, refrigerating, and storing donated citrated blood for later transfusion — and coined the term "blood bank," establishing that human blood could be preserved and stockpiled in advance of need rather than transfused only directly donor-to-patient.',
