        reason: 'The blood-bank concept spread rapidly: hospitals across the United States and Europe established their own banks, and the model was scaled massively for the Second World War, when the American Red Cross national blood-donor programme (begun 1941) collected and banked blood and plasma for military use. Stored, banked blood became standard transfusion practice worldwide, and the term Fantus coined entered universal medical and lay use.',
