    text: 'The claim that ordinary somatic cells could be reprogrammed into pluripotent "STAP" stem cells simply by exposing them to stress such as a mild acid bath — reported by Haruko Obokata of Japan\'s RIKEN institute in two Nature papers on 30 January 2014 — was found to rest on fabricated and manipulated data and was retracted.',
