    text: 'The OPERA collaboration\'s September 2011 report that neutrinos sent from CERN to the Gran Sasso laboratory in Italy arrived about 60 nanoseconds earlier than light would — apparently travelling faster than the speed of light — was reversed in 2012 when the anomaly was traced to a loose fibre-optic cable and a faulty clock.',
