        reason: 'On 23 September 2011 the OPERA collaboration announced, in a seminar at CERN and a preprint posted to arXiv, that muon neutrinos produced at CERN and detected 730 km away at the Gran Sasso National Laboratory appeared to arrive about 60 nanoseconds sooner than light, implying a velocity slightly above the speed of light at a reported six-sigma significance. The result, which if correct would have overturned special relativity, was deliberately released as a measurement requiring independent scrutiny, placing the extraordinary claim on the scientific record.',
