    text: 'In 1661 Robert Boyle published The Sceptical Chymist in London, rejecting the Aristotelian four elements and the Paracelsian three principles and instead defining elements as "perfectly unmingled bodies" not made of any others — an empirical, corpuscular definition that helped found modern chemistry.',
