        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Gregory X summoned the council partly to heal the schism of 1054. In the fourth session, on 6 July 1274, the Greek envoys of Michael VIII Palaiologos accepted papal primacy and the Filioque, and the union of the two churches was decreed and defined; the profession of faith and the conciliar constitutions were entered into the official acts of the council.',
