        reason: 'After Spanish forces stormed Vilcabamba in June 1572 and captured the young ruler, Viceroy Francisco de Toledo ordered Túpac Amaru tried and condemned. He was beheaded on a scaffold before the cathedral in Cusco\'s plaza before a crowd estimated in the thousands. The execution and its date were recorded by contemporaries, including the Dominican friar Gabriel de Oviedo, prior at Cusco, and the soldier-chronicler Baltasar de Ocampo, both of whom witnessed it.',
