    text: 'Atahualpa, the captive Inca emperor, was executed by garrote (strangulation) in the plaza of Cajamarca on 26 July 1533 on the orders of Francisco Pizarro, after his sentence of burning at the stake was commuted when he accepted Christian baptism.',
