        reason: 'On the plain of Panipat north of Delhi, Babur — outnumbered perhaps three or four to one — anchors his line behind a barricade of carts (the Ottoman "tulghuma" tactic), enfilades the Lodi host with his cannon and matchlocks, and envelops it with mounted archers. Ibrahim Lodi and some 15,000–20,000 of his men are killed on the field, among the earliest decisive use of gunpowder arms in the subcontinent. Babur records the battle in detail, day by day, in his own memoir, the Baburnama.',
