    text: 'On 5 September 2019 Shinde et al. published in Cell the first whole genome of an individual from the mature Indus Valley (Harappan) Civilisation, recovered from the Rakhigarhi cemetery, showing the person carried Iranian-related and South Asian hunter-gatherer ancestry but little or no Steppe pastoralist or Anatolian farmer ancestry.',
