        reason: 'At a prearranged signal during Easter Sunday Mass in the Duomo, the conspirators strike: Giuliano de\' Medici is stabbed nineteen times and dies at the altar, while Lorenzo, slashed in the neck, fights free and is barricaded into the sacristy by allies. The coup collapses when the Florentine populace rallies to the Medici rather than the plotters, and the conspirators — including Archbishop Salviati — are hanged from the windows of the Palazzo della Signoria within hours and days. The humanist Angelo Poliziano, present in the cathedral, set down an eyewitness account, the Pactianae coniurationis commentarium, and the apothecary Luca Landucci recorded the events in his Florentine diary.',
