        reason: 'The five-stone Karangtengah inscription, in Old Javanese and Sanskrit, opens with the date 746 Śaka (10th day of the dark fortnight, Kṛṣṇapakṣa, of the month Jyeṣṭha = 26 May 824 CE) and records under the Buddhist Śailendra house that King Samaratungga\'s daughter Pramodhawardhanī dedicated a Jinālaya (a sacred building of the Jina) and that a Venuvana ("bamboo grove") sanctuary was established for the cremated remains of a deceased king. The stone is the contemporaneous primary record of the endowment.',
