        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '0900-04-21',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'A thin copper plate is engraved with an official document that, opening with the date 822 Śaka (Monday, 21 April 900 CE), records that a chief acting on behalf of the ruler of Tundun (Tondo) acquits Namwaran and his descendants of a debt of one kati and eight suwarna of gold. The plate is the contemporaneous primary act of record — a legal release issued by an Indianised polity on Luzon, and the earliest dated written text from anywhere in the Philippine archipelago.',
