        reason: 'The plate was found in 1987 by a labourer dredging sand near the mouth of the Lumbang River in Laguna province and reached the National Museum of the Philippines. In 1991 the Dutch anthropologist Antoon Postma identified the script as Old Kawi and produced the first translation, reading the 21 April 900 CE date and the debt-release text, and publishing his commentary in Philippine Studies (1992). His decipherment established the inscription as the earliest calendar-dated Philippine document and as evidence of Luzon\'s integration into the wider Indianised world of maritime Southeast Asia; the reading and dating are settled in the scholarship.',
