        reason: 'Sent by the Yuan court of Temür Khan, Zhou Daguan reaches Angkor in the seventh lunar month (August) of 1296 and lives in the Khmer capital for some eleven months, observing the royal palace and processions, the temples, agriculture, trade, law, religion, and customs of the kingdom. On his return to China he composes the Zhenla fengtu ji, a detailed eyewitness record of the city while it was still a functioning capital — the only such firsthand account that survives.',
