    text: 'In 1293 a Yuan seaborne expedition sent by Kublai Khan landed on Java (22 January 1293) to punish its ruler; after the allied forces defeated Kediri at the Battle of Daha (26 April 1293), Raden Wijaya turned on the Mongols and ambushed them, forcing the Yuan army to withdraw from Java on 31 May 1293 — the only Mongol overseas expedition to maritime Southeast Asia, recorded in the History of Yuan.',
