    text: 'On March 16, 1966, Gemini 8, crewed by Neil Armstrong and David Scott, docked with an uncrewed Agena target vehicle in Earth orbit — the first docking of two spacecraft in orbit — before a stuck thruster forced an emergency undocking and the first crewed emergency landing of the U.S. space program.',
