        reason: 'About six hours after launch from Cape Kennedy, Armstrong manoeuvred Gemini 8 to within reach of the Agena Target Vehicle and gently nudged into its docking collar; the latches clicked and a green light confirmed the first docking of two spacecraft in orbit. Minutes later a stuck-open orbital-attitude thruster sent the joined craft into a violent roll; the crew undocked, regained control using the re-entry system, and made an emergency splashdown in the Pacific. NASA reported and logged the docking and the abort the same day.',
