        reason: 'Vasant Shinde, Vagheesh Narasimhan and colleagues recovered and sequenced ancient DNA from a Rakhigarhi skeleton roughly 4,600 years old and reported in Cell that the individual carried a mixture of Ancient Ancestral South Indian and Iranian-related hunter-gatherer ancestry, but no Steppe pastoralist and no Anatolian-farmer ancestry — the first published genome from the Indus Valley Civilisation, whose hot, humid sites had previously yielded no usable ancient DNA.',
