        toAxis: 'OPEN',
        community: 'SCHOLARLY',
        occurredAt: '2014-04-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'The genetic makeup of the people of the Indus Valley Civilisation was long unknown, because the hot climate of northwestern South Asia degrades ancient DNA and no Harappan genome had ever been sequenced. From April 2014 the Deccan College excavations at Rakhigarhi in Haryana recovered skeletal remains from the cemetery, opening the question of whether usable ancient DNA could be obtained and what ancestry it would reveal.',
