        fromAxis: 'OPEN',
        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'SCHOLARLY',
        occurredAt: '2019-10-17',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Shinde and colleagues, in "An Ancient Harappan Genome Lacks Ancestry from Steppe Pastoralists or Iranian Farmers" published in Cell (17 October 2019), reported the genome of an individual from Rakhigarhi mound RGR-7. The sample showed no Steppe-pastoralist ancestry — consistent with the arrival of Indo-Aryan-associated Steppe ancestry only after the decline of the Harappan civilisation — and no Anatolian-farmer ancestry, indicating a distinctive Indus-period gene pool. It was the first genome recovered from a Harappan individual.',
