    text: 'On 24 February 1871 Charles Darwin published The Descent of Man, and Selection in Relation to Sex, explicitly applying evolution by common descent to the human species, arguing that human mental and moral faculties differ from those of other animals in degree and not in kind, and introducing sexual selection as a mechanism shaping human and animal traits.',
