        occurredAt: '1871-02-24',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Having deliberately said almost nothing about human origins in On the Origin of Species (1859), Darwin set out the full case in The Descent of Man, published in two volumes by John Murray on 24 February 1871. He argued that humans descended from earlier animal forms by the same processes as other species, that human races share a common descent, and that sexual selection — competition and mate choice — explains many traits, including human secondary sexual characteristics, that natural selection alone does not.',
