        occurredAt: '1924-08-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'After the paper was rejected by the Philosophical Magazine, Bose sent his manuscript directly to Einstein in June 1924, asking him to arrange publication. Einstein immediately recognised its importance, translated it into German himself, and submitted it on Bose\'s behalf; it appeared as "Plancks Gesetz und Lichtquantenhypothese" in Zeitschrift für Physik (vol. 26, pp. 178–181, 1924). Bose had obtained Planck\'s law without invoking classical electrodynamics, treating photons as indistinguishable.',
