    externalId: 'trajectory:battle-of-the-aegates-241bce',
    text: 'On 10 March 241 BCE a Roman fleet under Gaius Lutatius Catulus destroyed the Carthaginian relief fleet under Hanno off the Aegates Islands west of Sicily, the final battle of the 23-year First Punic War, after which Carthage sued for peace and accepted the Treaty of Lutatius, surrendering Sicily and paying a large indemnity to Rome.',
