        toAxis: 'SETTLED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1996-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'Polybius, the closest surviving source, fixes the Aegates as the decisive action ending the First Punic War, a verdict carried by Diodorus and Eutropius and accepted in modern scholarship (J.F. Lazenby, "The First Punic War"). The identification has since been confirmed archaeologically: from 2004 the recovery of bronze warship rams, helmets, and amphorae from the seabed off Levanzo by the RPM Nautical Foundation and Sicilian authorities physically located the battle site. The date, outcome, and consequence — Carthage\'s loss of Sicily under the Treaty of Lutatius — are settled history.',
