    text: 'In late 1745 and early 1746 the Leyden jar — the first device able to accumulate and store a large electric charge for controlled discharge — was independently discovered by Ewald Georg von Kleist (October 1745) and by Pieter van Musschenbroek and Andreas Cunaeus at Leiden (January 1746).',
