        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'On 11 October 1745 the Pomeranian cleric Ewald Georg von Kleist accumulated charge in a medicine bottle filled with alcohol with a nail through the cork and received a violent shock; independently, in January 1746 Pieter van Musschenbroek and Andreas Cunaeus at Leiden produced the same effect with a water-filled glass jar. Musschenbroek communicated the discovery in a letter dated 20 January 1746 to René Antoine Ferchault de Réaumur, the first formal record of a device for storing electric charge.',
