        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2020-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'The Leyden jar was rapidly reproduced across Europe in 1746 — including the Abbé Nollet\'s famous demonstration discharging it through a line of linked people — and gave experimenters the first practical means of accumulating and preserving electric charge. It is recognised as the first capacitor and a foundational instrument of electrostatics, a point uncontested in the history of physics.',
