    text: 'On 18 June 860 a fleet of about 200 Rus\' vessels appeared without warning before Constantinople and ravaged its suburbs and the surrounding shores until withdrawing in early August; the raid produced the earliest contemporary written notice of the Rus\' people, recorded by the eyewitness Patriarch Photios of Constantinople.',
