    text: 'On 29 May 1555 the Ottoman Empire of Suleiman the Magnificent and Safavid Iran of Shah Tahmasp I signed the Peace of Amasya, the first formal peace treaty between the two empires; it ended the war of 1532–1555, partitioned Armenia and Georgia between them, confirmed Ottoman possession of most of Iraq including Baghdad, and guaranteed Persian pilgrims access to Mecca, Medina, and the Shia shrines of Iraq.',
