        fromAxis: 'RECORDED',
        toAxis: 'SETTLED',
        community: 'JUDICIAL',
        occurredAt: '2014-02-28',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'On 28 February 2014 chief executive Mark Karpelès filed for civil rehabilitation (bankruptcy protection) at the Tokyo District Court, reporting liabilities of about 6.5 billion yen against 3.84 billion yen in assets and stating that roughly 850,000 bitcoins — about 750,000 belonging to customers and 100,000 to the company, then worth around $450 million — had been lost to a mix of theft and security mismanagement. The court filing converted the collapse into a legally recorded insolvency; the recovery of some 200,000 bitcoins in an old wallet days later partially revised, but did not undo, the loss.',
