        reason: 'White, who had sailed for England in 1587 to fetch supplies and been delayed for three years by the Anglo-Spanish war, finally reached Roanoke Island on 18 August 1590 — his granddaughter Virginia Dare\'s birthday. He found the settlement abandoned, the dwellings taken down, chests of his belongings dug up and spoiled, and the letters "CRO" and the full word "CROATOAN" carved into a tree and a palisade post, but no cross of distress that would have signalled a forced departure. A storm drove his ships off before he could search Croatoan Island. White set down the discovery in his own narrative.',
