        reason: 'Despite four centuries of investigation — and modern archaeology by the First Colony Foundation at sites on Hatteras (Croatoan) Island and at "Site X" inland — no excavation or document has conclusively established what became of the roughly 115 Roanoke colonists. Assimilation into the Croatoan or other Indigenous communities is the leading hypothesis, but the fate of the colony remains unresolved, and the "Lost Colony" stands as one of the most durable open questions in early American history.',
