    externalId: 'trajectory:torres-strait-passage-1606',
    text: 'In late September–early October 1606 the Spanish navigator Luís Vaz de Torres sailed through the strait between New Guinea and the Australian mainland — proving New Guinea to be an island — but the discovery was buried in Spanish archives and remained unknown for over 150 years until Alexander Dalrymple recovered it and named the passage the Torres Strait.',
