        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Separated from Queirós\'s expedition, Torres took his ships from the New Hebrides westward along the southern coast of New Guinea, passing through the strait that now bears his name around 2–3 October 1606. He reported the passage in a memorial written to the Spanish Crown after reaching Manila (dated 1 June 1607). Because Spain treated Pacific discoveries as state secrets, the report was archived and not published, so the strait\'s existence stayed unknown to other navigators.',
