        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1762-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'When the British captured Manila in 1762, the hydrographer Alexander Dalrymple examined Spanish documents and recovered the record of Torres\'s 1606 passage; he named the channel the "Torres Strait" in his 1767 account and supplied a chart to Joseph Banks. James Cook used the knowledge to pass through the strait in 1770, confirming that New Guinea and Australia are separate. The reality of Torres\'s passage is now settled in the historiography of Pacific exploration.',
