        occurredAt: '1769-10-09',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Having observed the transit of Venus at Tahiti, the Endeavour reached the coast of New Zealand and on 9 October 1769 Cook went ashore on the eastern bank of the Tūranganui River. The meeting with the people of Ngāti Oneone and Rongowhakaata broke down into violence: over the four days in the bay several Māori were shot and killed or wounded. Cook named the place Poverty Bay because it "afforded us nothing we wanted." The landing and the deadly encounter were recorded contemporaneously in the journals of Cook and the naturalist Joseph Banks.',
