    text: 'On 5 October 1877 Chief Joseph surrendered the Nez Perce (Nimíipuu) to the US Army at the Bear Paw Mountains in Montana Territory, some 40 miles short of the Canadian border, ending the Nez Perce War and a fighting retreat of more than 1,000 miles — a surrender remembered for the speech recorded as "From where the sun now stands, I will fight no more forever."',
