    text: 'On 7 January 1822, printer Elisha Loomis pulled the first sheets of a pīʻāpā (spelling-book primer) on the mission press at Honolulu — the first time the previously oral Hawaiian language was committed to print, and the first printing done in the Hawaiian Islands.',
