    text: 'On 3 March 1832 the United States Supreme Court decided Worcester v. Georgia, holding that the Cherokee Nation was a distinct political community within which the laws of Georgia had no force and that authority over relations with the Indian nations belonged exclusively to the federal government — Chief Justice John Marshall\'s foundational statement of tribal sovereignty in American law.',
