        reason: 'The Court, in an opinion delivered by Chief Justice John Marshall on 3 March 1832, reversed the conviction of the missionary Samuel Worcester, who had been imprisoned under a Georgia statute requiring white persons living in Cherokee territory to obtain a state licence and oath. Marshall held the Cherokee Nation to be "a distinct community, occupying its own territory ... in which the laws of Georgia can have no force," and that the Constitution committed all intercourse with the Indian nations to the United States, not the individual states. The decision was reported in the official record of the term.',
