        reason: 'The sack of Kororāreka began the Flagstaff War (Northern War) of 1845–46 between Ngāpuhi and the Crown, fought through the engagements at Puketutu, Ōhaeawai and Ruapekapeka. Historians of the New Zealand Wars treat the date, the felling of the flagstaff, and the destruction of the town as settled facts, drawn from contemporary dispatches, missionary letters and Māori accounts, even as the war\'s causes and outcome are interpreted in various ways.',
