        reason: 'Best, commanding the Red Dragon and Hosiander, engaged the squadron of the Portuguese captain-major Nuno da Cunha in the roadstead off Swally near Surat on 29–30 November 1612 (New Style), driving off the far larger Portuguese force. The victory, witnessed by the governor of Gujarat, persuaded the Mughal authorities to favour English over Portuguese traders; on 6 January 1613 Best received a confirmed firman granting trading privileges at Surat. The action is recorded contemporaneously in the East India Company\'s shipboard journals and voyage narratives.',
