    text: 'On 9 June 1716 Banda Singh Bahadur, the Sikh military commander who had carved out the first Sikh-ruled state in the Punjab, was tortured and executed in Delhi on the orders of the Mughal emperor Farrukhsiyar after his capture at Gurdas Nangal the previous December.',
