        reason: 'After the Mughals starved out his garrison and captured him at Gurdas Nangal on 7 December 1715, Banda Singh Bahadur was paraded to Delhi with hundreds of followers, who were executed in batches over the spring. On 9 June 1716 Banda himself was put to death — his young son killed before him, his eyes gouged out, his flesh torn with hot pincers, and his body dismembered. The mass executions and Banda\'s death were observed and reported by a European agent of the British East India Company resident at the Mughal court.',
