        reason: 'Avenging the death of his son Lourenço at Chaul the previous year, Almeida brought his fleet against the allied galleys and carracks anchored at Diu under the Mamluk admiral Mir Husain and the Gujarati governor Malik Ayyaz. Portuguese broadside gunnery shattered the Muslim fleet, sinking or capturing the Mamluk ships at a fraction of the enemy\'s casualties. The battle is recorded in the near-contemporary Portuguese chronicles of Fernão Lopes de Castanheda and Gaspar Correia and in the Persian Gujarati history Mirat-i-Sikandari.',
