        reason: 'After a government study of official documents and interviews with former comfort women, Chief Cabinet Secretary Yōhei Kōno read a statement on 4 August 1993 conceding that the military had been "directly or indirectly" involved in the comfort stations, that recruitment was at times carried out coercively and against the women\'s will, and expressing apology and remorse. The admission reversed Japan\'s earlier official position that the stations were privately run and free of state coercion.',
