        reason: 'Edited by John Faithfull Fleet in Inscriptions of the Early Gupta Kings (Corpus Inscriptionum Indicarum vol. III, 1888, no. 11), the inscription\'s date and reading are settled in Gupta epigraphy. As one of the latest securely dated records of Kumāragupta I, it is regularly cited both as a fixed point in his chronology and, on account of its use of the title mahārāja, in discussions of the reverses the dynasty faced toward the end of his reign.',
