        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Brielle et al., "Entwined African and Asian genetic roots of medieval peoples of the Swahili coast," published in Nature on 29 March 2023, report genome-wide data from 80 individuals (54 newly sequenced) buried at six Swahili towns between roughly ad 1250 and 1800. The genomes show large, sometimes majority, Asian ancestry that is about 80–90% Persian on the male line and predominantly African on the female line, with admixture beginning by about ad 1000 — matching the Islamization of the coast and giving the long-disputed "Shirazi" origin tradition an empirical genetic basis while affirming the population\'s deep African roots.',
