    text: 'Roman forces under the future emperor Titus stormed Jerusalem and burned the Second Temple on the tenth day of the month Lous (Av), in the late summer of 70 CE, ending the sacrificial cult and the First Jewish–Roman War — an event recorded by the eyewitness participant Flavius Josephus, who noted it fell on the same calendar day the First Temple had been burnt by the king of Babylon.',
