        occurredAt: '0070-08-30',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Josephus, a Jewish commander who surrendered to the Romans and witnessed the siege from Titus\'s camp, records in The Jewish War that as the legions fought into the Temple courts a soldier hurled a brand into the sanctuary and the building was consumed by fire. He fixes the day: "it was the tenth day of the month Lous, [Ab,] upon which it was formerly burnt by the king of Babylon." His narrative, written within a decade of the event, is the contemporaneous record of the Temple\'s destruction.',
