    text: 'Judas Maccabeus and his followers, having driven the Seleucid garrison from the Temple Mount, built a new altar and rededicated the Temple in Jerusalem, resuming the daily sacrifice at dawn on the twenty-fifth day of the month Kislev in the year 148 of the Seleucid era (mid-December 164 BCE) — three years after Antiochus IV had defiled it — and ordained an annual eight-day festival, observed ever since as Hanukkah.',
