        reason: '1 Maccabees, composed in Judea within about two generations of the events, records the rededication precisely: "Early in the morning on the twenty-fifth day of the ninth month, which is the month of Chislev, in the one hundred forty-eighth year, they rose and offered sacrifice, as the law directs, on the new altar of burnt offering that they had built." It adds that Judas and the assembly decreed the rededication be kept "with gladness and joy for eight days" each year — the founding record of the festival of Hanukkah.',
