        occurredAt: '1957-09-29',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'A cooling-system failure in a buried stainless-steel tank holding tens of tonnes of high-level radioactive waste allowed the contents to overheat and detonate chemically with a force estimated at 70–100 tonnes of TNT, blasting off the concrete lid and releasing some 20 million curies of radioactivity. A plume contaminated more than 50,000 square kilometres along what became the East Urals Radioactive Trace, and roughly 10,000 people were eventually evacuated. The explosion and its consequences were recorded internally by the closed Soviet nuclear establishment but withheld from the public.',
