        reason: 'The disaster was kept secret for decades: the area was erased from maps and the existence of the Mayak complex itself was classified. The Soviet dissident biologist Zhores Medvedev first revealed the catastrophe in the West in New Scientist in 1976, but Soviet authorities denied it until — several years after Chernobyl — they began declassifying documents on the accident in 1989. The date, cause, scale, and INES-6 severity are now documented in the released archives and the full scientific literature and are uncontested settled fact.',
