        reason: 'Soyuz 1, launched on 23 April 1967 and beset by failures in orbit, was ordered to return early. During descent on 24 April the main parachute did not unfold and the reserve chute tangled with the drogue, so the capsule struck the ground in Orenburg Oblast at roughly 40 m/s; Komarov died of multiple blunt-force injuries. Unlike many Soviet space mishaps, his death was announced and he was given a state funeral, placing the first in-flight spaceflight fatality on the public record.',
