    text: 'On 30 October 1961 the Soviet Union detonated the RDS-220 hydrogen bomb ("Tsar Bomba") over the Sukhoy Nos cape of Novaya Zemlya in the Russian Arctic, yielding roughly 50 megatons of TNT — the most powerful nuclear weapon ever tested and the single largest man-made explosion in history.',
