        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'A Tu-95V bomber released the device, deliberately downrated from a ~100-megaton design to about 50 megatons, over the Mityushikha Bay testing range (Sukhoy Nos, Zone C) on Novaya Zemlya; it detonated by barometric trigger at about 4,000 m at 11:32 Moscow time. The fireball reached the ground and was seen and felt for hundreds of kilometres, the mushroom cloud rose to some 60 km, and the blast shattered windows as far away as Norway and Finland. Nikita Khrushchev had foreshadowed a "50-megaton" test in his 17 October speech to the 22nd Party Congress, and the explosion was instrumented internally by the Soviet weapons programme and immediately detected by Western atmospheric and seismic monitoring.',
