    text: 'On 19 August 1989 a border gate on the Austro-Hungarian frontier near Sopron, Hungary was opened for a few hours during the "Pan-European Picnic," and several hundred East German citizens fled across to the West — the first mass breach of the Iron Curtain and a catalyst for the collapse of the East German regime.',
