    text: 'On 26 June 2014 the Supreme Court of Canada, in Tsilhqot\'in Nation v British Columbia, for the first time granted a declaration of Aboriginal title to a specific tract of land — about 1,750 square kilometres in the interior of British Columbia — recognising the Tsilhqot\'in Nation\'s exclusive right to use and control the territory.',
