    externalId: 'trajectory:ngati-apa-foreshore-seabed-2003',
    text: 'On 19 June 2003 the New Zealand Court of Appeal, in Attorney-General v Ngati Apa, held that Māori customary title to the foreshore and seabed had survived the assumption of British sovereignty and could be investigated by the Māori Land Court — overturning the 1963 ruling in In re the Ninety-Mile Beach that such customary title had been extinguished.',
