        toAxis: 'CONTESTED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2005-01-04',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Jared Diamond\'s book "Collapse: How Societies Choose to Fail or Succeed" (published 4 January 2005) popularises the "ecocide" model of Rapa Nui, in which the islanders deforested their environment, exhausted its resources, and suffered a catastrophic self-inflicted population collapse in the seventeenth or eighteenth century before Europeans arrived. The model becomes the dominant popular narrative of the island, while archaeologists increasingly dispute whether any such pre-contact crash occurred — leaving the question of a demographic collapse genuinely contested.',
