        occurredAt: '1756-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'In the aftermath the prime minister Sebastião José de Carvalho e Melo (later Marquis of Pombal) ordered the collection of factual data, sending a standardized questionnaire to every parish in the kingdom asking about the timing of the shock, the direction of the tremors, sea-level changes, casualties and fire damage. The priests\' answers, archived in the Torre do Tombo, let modern scientists reconstruct the event; because Pombal was the first to attempt a large-scale objective investigation of an earthquake, he is regarded as a forerunner of modern seismology.',
