        reason: 'Foucault presented his note "Démonstration physique du mouvement de rotation de la Terre au moyen du pendule" to the Académie des sciences on 3 February 1851; it appeared in the Comptes rendus (tome 32, p. 135). A long, heavy pendulum, once set swinging, keeps its plane of oscillation fixed in space while the Earth turns beneath it, so the plane appears to rotate — providing the first simple terrestrial proof of diurnal rotation, ending two centuries of search for a direct experimental demonstration.',
