        occurredAt: '2003-02-05',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'On 5 February 2003 US Secretary of State Colin Powell addressed the UN Security Council, presenting intelligence — including audio intercepts, satellite imagery, and the assertion that Iraq held biological and chemical agents and was reconstituting its nuclear programme — to argue that Saddam Hussein retained an active arsenal of weapons of mass destruction. The claim, echoed by US and British government dossiers, was placed on the international record as the principal casus belli for the invasion that began on 20 March 2003.',
