        fromAxis: 'RECORDED',
        toAxis: 'CONTESTED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2013-11-06',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'After Arafat\'s body was exhumed in Ramallah on 27 November 2012 and sampled by French, Swiss and Russian teams, the Swiss forensic institute in Lausanne reported on 6 November 2013 that his ribs and pelvis carried polonium-210 levels far above normal and that the results "moderately supported" the hypothesis of poisoning by the radioactive isotope. The finding gave scientific weight to the poisoning allegation and sharpened, rather than closed, the dispute over how Arafat died.',
