        reason: 'The Fasti Triumphales record the triumph of L. Cornelius Balbus "ex Africa" on the sixth day before the Kalends of April (vi K. April. = 27 March) of 19 BCE — the last triumph granted to a Roman outside the imperial family. His campaign against the Garamantes of the Fezzan reached far into the desert; Pliny the Elder (Naturalis Historia 5.36–37) preserves the names of the towns, rivers, and peoples displayed on the triumphal placards, the earliest concrete Roman knowledge of the Saharan interior and its trans-desert routes.',
