        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'PUBLIC',
        occurredAt: '1574-11-29',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'On the eve of Saint Andrew\'s Day, 29 November 1574, Limahong\'s fleet appeared off Manila Bay and landed a vanguard under the Japanese captain Sioco, who pressed toward the town and killed the Spanish field marshal Martín de Goiti in his house. A renewed assault the next day, 30 November, was thrown back by the small garrison rallied by Juan de Salcedo; the pirates lost heavily and retreated to their ships, then sailed north to establish a base at the Agno River in Pangasinan. The attack on the three-year-old Spanish capital was reported at once to the crown.',
