        reason: 'The contemporaneous Spanish relations — chiefly Governor Francisco de Sande\'s 1576 report and the accounts gathered in Blair and Robertson\'s The Philippine Islands, 1493–1898 (1903–1909) — fix the date, the death of Goiti, and the successful defence by Salcedo. Modern historiography of the early Spanish Philippines treats the November 1574 attack and its repulse as settled fact: the colony\'s survival and the subsequent pursuit of Limahong to Pangasinan in 1575 are uncontested, while only the pirate\'s later fate remains obscure.',
