        occurredAt: '1641-01-14',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'A VOC fleet blockaded Malacca from 3 August 1640 while Dutch and Johor land forces invested the Portuguese citadel of A Famosa. After months in which disease killed several Dutch commanders, the final assault on 14 January 1641 — led by Sergeant Major Johannes Lamotius because the commander Minne Willemszoon Caertekoe lay sick — carried the fortress; the surviving garrison and Portuguese captain-major surrendered. The conquest is documented in the VOC\'s dispatches and siege journals sent to the Heren XVII and to Batavia.',
