    text: 'In June 1596 the four ships of the first Dutch expedition to the East Indies, under Cornelis de Houtman, reached the pepper port of Banten (Bantam) on Java — the first Dutch voyage to the archipelago, which despite heavy losses proved the route and launched the trade that would become the Dutch East India Company.',
