        reason: 'The expedition mounted by the Compagnie van Verre had sailed from Amsterdam in April 1595 and, after a voyage that killed much of the crew from scurvy and internal strife, reached Banten in June 1596 — the first Dutch ships to reach the Indonesian archipelago, breaking the Portuguese monopoly on the spice route. The voyage was recorded day by day in the journal kept by the merchant Willem Lodewycksz, published in 1598 as D\'Eerste Boeck.',
