        reason: 'Yolngu plaintiffs — led by Milirrpum Marika of the Rirratjingu clan, with Mungurrawuy Yunupingu of the Gumatj and others — sue Nabalco and the Commonwealth over bauxite mining on the Gove Peninsula in Arnhem Land, asking the court to recognise their traditional ownership. In the first litigated test of Aboriginal land rights in an Australian court, Justice Blackburn finds that the Yolngu have a recognisable system of law but holds that the common law of Australia does not recognise communal native title; he rules against the plaintiffs. The judgment is handed down and reported as the leading authority on the question.',
