        occurredAt: '0612-08-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'The Babylonian chronicle now known as the Fall of Nineveh Chronicle records, year by year, the campaigns of Nabopolassar against Assyria. Under his fourteenth year it states that the king of Akkad and Cyaxares the Mede marched against Nineveh, laid siege from the month of Simanu, and in the month of Abu carried out "a great defeat of the people," took the city, turned it into a ruin-mound, and that the Assyrian king Sin-shar-ishkun perished. It is a dated, non-narrative civic record kept by Babylonian temple scribes, fixing the destruction to the Babylonian calendar.',
