        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '1955-11-22',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'After the staged "Sloika" device RDS-6s of 1953, Sakharov, Zeldovich and the Arzamas-16 team designed a genuine radiation-implosion two-stage weapon. The bomb, deliberately under-loaded to a 1.6-megaton yield, was dropped from a Tu-16 over the Semipalatinsk steppe and detonated at about 1,550 m. A temperature inversion focused the shock wave back to the ground: a trench collapsed and killed a soldier, and a building in Kurchatov ~65 km away collapsed and killed a girl, with dozens injured by flying glass. The test and its date were logged in the Soviet weapons programme and detected abroad by atmospheric monitoring.',
