        reason: 'The two coalitions contesting control of Japan after the death of Toyotomi Hideyoshi meet in fog near the mountain pass of Sekigahara. The battle turns when Kobayakawa Hideaki, nominally of the Western Army, defects and attacks his own side; the Western Army collapses, Mitsunari flees and is later captured and executed. The engagement and its date are recorded in Japanese battle chronicles and contemporary correspondence.',
