        reason: 'Modern scholarship treats Sekigahara as the decisive battle that ended the Sengoku contest for Japan: Ieyasu redistributed the domains of the defeated, was appointed shōgun in 1603, and founded the Tokugawa shogunate that ruled until 1868. The date, outcome, and the role of Kobayakawa\'s defection are settled in the historiography of early-modern Japan.',
