    text: 'On 21 February 1978 electrical-company workers digging in the heart of Mexico City struck a 3.25-metre carved stone disk depicting the dismembered Mexica moon goddess Coyolxauhqui — a find that located the buried Templo Mayor of Tenochtitlan and launched the systematic excavation of the Aztec sacred precinct.',
