        reason: 'Ralph H. Fowler and Edward A. Milne at Cambridge refined and extended Saha\'s theory (1923–1924), placing the relation between spectral class and temperature on a rigorous quantitative footing and applying it across the stellar sequence. The Saha equation became the basis of Cecilia Payne\'s 1925 demonstration that stars are made chiefly of hydrogen, and remains a cornerstone of astrophysics and plasma physics.',
