    text: 'On 19 February 1937 (Yekatit 12 in the Ethiopian calendar), after two Eritreans threw grenades at the Italian viceroy Rodolfo Graziani in Addis Ababa, Italian soldiers and Blackshirts carried out a three-day massacre of the city\'s inhabitants, killing thousands of Ethiopians in the deadliest single atrocity of the Italian occupation.',
