        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'During an alms-giving ceremony at the Genete Leul Palace, Abraha Deboch and Mogus Asgedom hurl grenades at Viceroy Graziani, wounding him and others. In reprisal, Italian authorities give carte blanche to destroy and kill: over three days Italian troops, Fascist militia, and civilian colonists shoot, stab, burn, and bludgeon the population of Addis Ababa, with later mass executions of suspected resisters and the Debre Libanos monastery clergy. The massacre is documented at the time by foreign witnesses and diplomats and, despite Italian censorship, reported abroad.',
