        reason: 'Workers of the Compañía de Luz y Fuerza del Centro, laying underground cable at the corner of Guatemala and Argentina streets in the colonial centre of Mexico City, uncovered a large oval relief stone more than three metres across showing the decapitated and dismembered goddess Coyolxauhqui. Archaeologists of the Instituto Nacional de Antropología e Historia identified it as lying at the foot of the Templo Mayor of Tenochtitlan, fixing the temple\'s location beneath the modern city.',
