        occurredAt: '1968-10-02',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'As thousands gathered in the Plaza de las Tres Culturas at Tlatelolco, army and police units surrounding the square opened fire; the shooting, begun around 6:15 p.m., continued into the night, and the government detained large numbers of demonstrators. Mexican newspapers the next morning, 3 October 1968, reported the official account of roughly 20 to 28 dead — a figure the government maintained for decades.',
