        occurredAt: '2000-07-06',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Drafted in response to President Thabo Mbeki\'s engagement with AIDS denialists and his questioning of the link between HIV and AIDS, the Durban Declaration was published in Nature on 6 July 2000 with more than 5,000 signatories, each required to hold a Ph.D. or M.D.-equivalent degree. It stated that the evidence that HIV causes AIDS is "clear-cut, exhaustive and unambiguous," formally consolidating the scientific consensus on the eve of the Durban AIDS conference.',
