        reason: 'Overnight on 14–15 April 2014, armed men raided the Government Girls Secondary School in Chibok and drove off with roughly 276 students; about 57 escaped by jumping from the vehicles in the first hours. In the days that followed the number taken, their whereabouts, and the perpetrators\' identity were uncertain and disputed — the Nigerian military at one point wrongly claimed most of the girls had been freed — while the #BringBackOurGirls hashtag, created in April 2014, made the case a global cause.',
