        reason: 'Responsibility for firing the missiles remains disputed between the two principal theories — that Hutu Power extremists shot the plane down to derail the Arusha peace process, or that the Tutsi-led Rwandan Patriotic Front did so to seize power. On 17 November 2006 the French magistrate Jean-Louis Bruguière issued arrest warrants blaming the RPF and Paul Kagame; Rwanda\'s own multivolume Mutsinzi report (2010) and a French ballistics study made public in January 2012 instead pointed to a launch site inside government-held Kanombe barracks, implicating Hutu extremists. No investigation has produced a verdict accepted by all sides, and the question is still open.',
