        reason: 'Two papers in Nature, led by Haruko Obokata of the RIKEN Center for Developmental Biology in Kobe with co-authors including Charles Vacanti and Teruhiko Wakayama, reported that exposing differentiated mouse cells to a low-pH stress bath could turn them back into pluripotent "STAP" stem cells — a startlingly simple alternative to iPS cell methods. The claim was hailed as a potential breakthrough and entered the scientific record, with RIKEN holding press conferences promoting the result.',
