        reason: 'After sailing up the East African coast and being met with hostility at Mombasa on 7 April 1498, da Gama\'s ships reached the rival port of Malindi on 14 April, where the sultan — eager for an ally against Mombasa — received the Portuguese warmly and provided a pilot who used his knowledge of the monsoon to bring the fleet to Calicut. The encounters at Mozambique, Mombasa, and Malindi were set down day by day in the anonymous shipboard journal (Roteiro), traditionally attributed to Álvaro Velho, the first European documentary record of the Swahili coast.',
