        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2006-09-15',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The block was recovered by villagers quarrying gravel from a mound at Lomas de Tacamichapa, near the Olmec capital of San Lorenzo, and reported to archaeologists who tied it by associated potsherds and figurine fragments to the San Lorenzo phase, before about 900 BCE. Rodríguez Martínez, Houston and colleagues published it as "Oldest Writing in the New World" in Science, recording the 62-sign sequence — arranged in horizontal rows and reusing distinct elements like a true script — on the scientific register.',
