    text: 'On 17 December 1970 Polish army and militia units fired into crowds of workers on the Baltic coast — most lethally at the Gdynia rail station as men arrived for the morning shift — during a wave of strikes that began on 14 December against sudden food-price rises; at least 44 people were killed across Gdańsk, Gdynia, Szczecin and Elbląg.',
