        reason: 'Hutton\'s expanded two-volume "Theory of the Earth" (1795) and its deep-time, cyclic vision were attacked by catastrophists and by those committed to a young Earth and a defining biblical Deluge. Critics including Richard Kirwan charged the theory with atheistic implications; the indefinite antiquity of the Earth and the absence of a creation event remained actively disputed through the early nineteenth century.',
