    text: 'In November 1977 Carl Woese and George Fox published "Phylogenetic structure of the prokaryotic domain," reporting that archaebacteria (Archaea) constitute a third primary line of descent as distinct from bacteria as either is from eukaryotes, overturning the two-kingdom prokaryote/eukaryote division of life.',
