        occurredAt: '1977-11-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'Using comparative cataloguing of 16S ribosomal RNA sequences, Woese and Fox reported in PNAS (74(11):5088–5090) that the methanogenic "archaebacteria" form a group as distinct from ordinary bacteria as bacteria are from eukaryotes, comprising "a third kingdom" of life. The finding directly challenged the long-settled view that all cellular life divided into just two categories, prokaryotes and eukaryotes, and was initially met with widespread skepticism.',
