        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1990-06-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'As ribosomal-RNA and genomic data accumulated, the distinctness of the Archaea was confirmed, and in 1990 Woese, Otto Kandler, and Mark Wheelis formalized the three-domain system (Bacteria, Archaea, Eucarya) in PNAS. The three-domain classification of life became the standard framework in microbiology and evolutionary biology.',
