        occurredAt: '1986-06-06',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The Presidential Commission chaired by William Rogers, formed 6 February 1986, published its report on 6 June 1986 concluding that the accident was caused by hot gas blowing past O-rings in a field joint of the right solid rocket booster, whose faulty design was unacceptably sensitive to the low launch-day temperature that stiffened the rubber seals. Physicist Richard Feynman\'s ice-water O-ring demonstration made the finding vivid. The O-ring cause is the settled engineering conclusion of the disaster.',
