        reason: 'Passed by the 31st Congress as part of the Compromise of 1850 and signed into law by President Millard Fillmore on 18 September 1850, the Act required that escaped slaves be returned to claimants on as little as a sworn statement of ownership, obliged citizens and federal marshals everywhere to assist on pain of fine and imprisonment, and barred the accused from a jury trial or from testifying. It entered the United States Statutes at Large (9 Stat. 462) as binding federal law.',
