        occurredAt: '2023-12-13',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'At the close of the 28th Conference of the Parties, hosted by the United Arab Emirates in Dubai, nearly 200 nations adopt the first Global Stocktake decision under the Paris Agreement. The text — branded the "UAE Consensus" — calls on parties to contribute to "transitioning away from fossil fuels in energy systems, in a just, orderly and equitable manner", to triple renewable energy capacity, and to reach net zero by 2050. It is the first UNFCCC outcome in nearly three decades of climate negotiations to name fossil fuels as the cause of climate change.',
