    text: 'A brilliant comet (perihelion 23 March 1066) blazed in the sky in the spring of 1066, in the months before the Norman Conquest of England; it was recorded in the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, witnessed by the monk Eilmer of Malmesbury, and later embroidered into the Bayeux Tapestry as an omen, and was subsequently identified as an apparition of the periodic comet 1P/Halley.',
