        reason: 'Observing from Bremen on 29 March 1807, the physician-astronomer Heinrich Wilhelm Olbers found a new moving point of light in the constellation Virgo — the fourth small body discovered between Mars and Jupiter, after Ceres (1801), Pallas (1802) and Juno (1804). He had been deliberately scanning the regions where the orbits of Pallas and Ceres crossed, on the conjecture that such bodies might be fragments of a single shattered planet. He invited Carl Friedrich Gauss, whose orbit methods had recovered Ceres, to name the new object, which Gauss called Vesta.',
