        reason: 'Entropy and the second law became foundational to physics. Ludwig Boltzmann\'s statistical interpretation of entropy as a measure of microscopic disorder (1877) connected Clausius\'s thermodynamic quantity to the molecular theory of matter, and entropy now anchors thermodynamics, statistical mechanics and information theory. Clausius\'s definition, name and formulation of the second law are settled science.',
