    text: 'On the morning of 15 September 1963, Ku Klux Klan members bombed the 16th Street Baptist Church in Birmingham, Alabama, killing four Black girls — Addie Mae Collins, Carol Denise McNair, Carole Robertson and Cynthia Wesley — an atrocity whose perpetrators went uncharged for years and were convicted only across decades of reopened prosecutions.',
