        reason: 'Historians regard Nördlingen as among the most important battles of the Thirty Years\' War: it ended Swedish dominance in the south, drove the German Protestant states to the Treaty of Prague (May 1635), and prompted France to declare war on Spain in May 1635, broadening the conflict into a Franco-Habsburg struggle lasting to 1659. The date, combatants and outcome are settled history.',
