    externalId: 'trajectory:council-sens-abelard-condemnation-1141',
    text: 'At the Council of Sens, held on the octave of Pentecost (around 25 May 1141), Bernard of Clairvaux secured the condemnation of a list of theological propositions drawn from Peter Abelard\'s writings; Pope Innocent II confirmed the condemnation by letters of 16 July 1141, ordering Abelard\'s books burned and imposing perpetual silence on him — a landmark moment in the twelfth-century conflict between dialectical reason and monastic authority.',
