        reason: 'On 16 July 1141 Pope Innocent II ratified the council\'s findings, condemning Abelard\'s doctrines as heretical, ordering his books burned, excommunicating his followers, and sentencing both Abelard and his disciple Arnold of Brescia to perpetual silence. Through the mediation of Peter the Venerable, abbot of Cluny, Abelard was reconciled with Bernard and the Church and died at a Cluniac priory in April 1142. Modern scholarship treats the council and its papal confirmation as settled events — debating the exact day and the year (1140 versus the now-favoured 1141) but not the fact of the condemnation, which fixed the limits placed on dialectical theology before the rise of the universities.',
