        toAxis: 'SETTLED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1987-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'Later scholarship — beginning with Robert Conquest\'s The Harvest of Sorrow (1986) and the U.S. Commission on the Ukraine Famine (1988), and reinforced by post-Soviet archival access in the 1990s — confirmed that a man-made famine killed millions in 1932–33, vindicating Jones\'s reporting. Ukraine and many other states have since recognised the Holodomor as a genocide, and in 2003 the New York Times itself acknowledged Duranty\'s reporting as "some of the worst" in the paper\'s history. Jones\'s account is now treated as substantially accurate.',
