        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '1945-06-11',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The Committee on the Social and Political Implications of the atomic bomb — James Franck (chairman), Leó Szilárd, Eugene Rabinowitch, Glenn Seaborg, Donald Hughes, J. J. Nickson and J. C. Stearns — completed its report at the University of Chicago on 11 June 1945. It argued that a surprise atomic bombing of Japan would forfeit U.S. moral standing and trigger an uncontrollable arms race, and urged a demonstration of the weapon before United Nations representatives on a desert or barren island instead. Franck carried it to Washington on 12 June; the Interim Committee\'s Scientific Panel reviewed and set it aside.',
