        reason: 'Commissioned by Himmler to quantify the progress of the "Final Solution," statistician Richard Korherr submitted his report on 23 March 1943. It tabulated a decline of roughly four million in Europe\'s Jewish population between 1937 and the end of 1942 and recorded 1,274,166 Jews "processed" (durchgeschleust) through the camps of the General Government and 145,301 through the Warthegau. At Himmler\'s explicit instruction the euphemism "Sonderbehandlung" (special treatment) was replaced with "durchgeschleust" in the abridged version prepared for Hitler — a deliberate obscuring of mass murder preserved in the documentary record.',
