    text: 'In a paper published in Nature on 20 December 1947 (vol. 160, pp. 855–857), George Rochester and Clifford Butler of the University of Manchester reported two cloud-chamber photographs of cosmic-ray events showing forked "V" tracks — a neutral particle decaying into two charged pions and a charged particle decaying into a pion plus a neutral — the first evidence of the new unstable particles later identified as kaons, opening the era of "strange particle" physics.',
