        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1985-11-14',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Over eleven days in September 1985 the Rice/Sussex team used a pulsed laser to vaporise graphite into a helium stream and found a dominant mass peak at 720 daltons (60 carbon atoms). Reasoning that only a closed cage could account for the cluster\'s stability, they proposed the truncated-icosahedron structure and named it after Buckminster Fuller\'s geodesic domes. Their paper "C60: Buckminsterfullerene" appeared in Nature on 14 November 1985.',
