    text: 'In 1981 Gerd Binnig and Heinrich Rohrer at IBM\'s Zürich Research Laboratory built the scanning tunneling microscope (STM), which exploits the quantum tunneling current between a sharp conducting tip and a surface to image individual atoms — the first instrument capable of resolving the atomic-scale topography of conducting surfaces in real space.',
