        reason: 'In March 1999 Kaw Bing Chua and colleagues at the University of Malaya isolated a new virus from the cerebrospinal fluid of a patient from Sungai Nipah village, growing it in Vero cell culture and showing by electron microscopy and serology that it was a paramyxovirus closely related to — but distinct from — the Australian Hendra virus. The CDC and University of Malaya jointly reported the new agent, named "Nipah" after the village; the recognition redirected control away from mosquitoes toward the culling of more than a million pigs that ended the outbreak.',
