        occurredAt: '1215-08-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'Acting under authority delegated by Pope Innocent III, the cardinal-legate Robert de Courçon drew up a set of regulations for the masters and scholars of Paris, dated in the document itself "in the year of grace 1215, in the month of August." They set the qualifications and minimum age for masters of arts, ordered the texts to be read (Aristotle\'s old and new logic), and renewed the 1210 prohibition on lecturing publicly on Aristotle\'s natural philosophy and metaphysics — the earliest comprehensive written constitution of the nascent university. The text is preserved in the Chartularium Universitatis Parisiensis.',
