    text: 'On 9 December 1968, at the Fall Joint Computer Conference in San Francisco, Douglas Engelbart of Stanford Research Institute gave a 90-minute live demonstration — later nicknamed "The Mother of All Demos" — that publicly introduced the computer mouse, hypertext links, real-time collaborative editing, windows, and video-conferencing, demonstrating interactive networked computing decades before such tools became commonplace.',
