    externalId: 'trajectory:slim-pinpoint-moon-landing-2024',
    text: 'On 19 January 2024 (20 January JST) JAXA\'s Smart Lander for Investigating Moon (SLIM) touched down near Shioli crater, making Japan the fifth nation to soft-land an operational spacecraft on the Moon and demonstrating the first pinpoint lunar landing — within about 100 m of its target — even though the lander came to rest on its nose with its solar cells facing the wrong way.',
