        occurredAt: '2024-01-19',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'At 15:20 UTC on 19 January 2024 (00:20 JST, 20 January) SLIM made a soft landing near Shioli crater and re-established communications, making Japan the fifth country — after the Soviet Union, the United States, China and India — to soft-land an operational spacecraft on the Moon. An anomaly during descent left the lander resting on its nose with its solar cells unable to generate power, so whether the precision objective had been met was not yet established.',
