    text: 'The English Bill of Rights (1 Will & Mar Sess 2 c 2) received royal assent on 16 December 1689, enacting as statute the Declaration of Right that Parliament had presented to William and Mary in February 1689 — limiting the powers of the Crown, affirming the rights of Parliament and subjects, and settling the Protestant succession after the Glorious Revolution.',
