    externalId: 'trajectory:galileo-neptune-observation-1612',
    text: 'On 28 December 1612, and again on 27 January 1613, Galileo Galilei plotted the planet Neptune as a faint fixed star in his notebook while tracking Jupiter\'s moons — an unrecognised pre-discovery observation, made 234 years before Neptune was identified as a planet in 1846, that his drawings place exactly where Neptune then stood.',
