        reason: 'While observing the four Galilean moons of Jupiter, Galileo noted a nearby object he took to be a fixed star; his observation drawings of 28 December 1612 and 27 January 1613 (New Style) record plotted points that match the computed positions of Neptune on those dates. Because Neptune had just turned retrograde and was nearly stationary, its motion was too slight for his telescope to reveal, so he entered it as a star and did not recognise it as a planet.',
