        reason: 'In 1980 Charles Kowal and Stillman Drake re-examined Galileo\'s surviving observation notebooks and showed that the points he had drawn coincide with the calculated positions of Neptune on 28 December 1612 and 27 January 1613, establishing the earliest known telescopic record of the planet. A 2009 analysis further argued that Galileo may have noted the object had shifted relative to a neighbouring star. The pre-discovery observation is now an accepted footnote to Neptune\'s formal discovery in September 1846.',
