    text: 'In late 1877 Thomas Edison built the first phonograph — a tinfoil-cylinder machine that both recorded and reproduced sound — demonstrating it on 29 November 1877 and receiving US Patent 200,521 on 19 February 1878; it was the first device to capture and replay the human voice.',
