        reason: 'Having conceived between May and July 1877 that the indentations made by a vibrating stylus on a moving surface could be used to reproduce sound, Edison had his machinist John Kruesi build a hand-cranked cylinder wrapped in tinfoil. Edison recited "Mary had a little lamb" into the mouthpiece and the machine played the words back. The working device was demonstrated on 29 November 1877 and shown to the editors of Scientific American, who reported it in December 1877.',
