        reason: 'Perrier and Segrè proposed the name "technetium" (from the Greek technetos, "artificial") in Nature in January 1947, and the name was subsequently adopted by IUPAC. By then the element\'s isotopes were well characterised and it was firmly established as the first synthetic element; its discovery anchored the modern understanding that the periodic table could be completed by artificial nucleosynthesis.',
