        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1939-09-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'Searching for a cheap, durable contact insecticide harmless to plants and warm-blooded animals, Müller tested hundreds of compounds. In September 1939 — after some 349 prior failures — he found that DDT killed flies on contact and persisted on treated surfaces, remaining lethal to a wide range of insects. The compound had been synthesised by Othmar Zeidler in 1874, but Zeidler never recognised its insecticidal value. Geigy filed a Swiss patent in 1940.',
