        reason: 'Milgram ran many variants over the following years and synthesised them in his 1974 book Obedience to Authority; the core finding — high rates of destructive obedience to authority under laboratory conditions — has been reproduced in numerous later studies, including Jerry Burger\'s partial replication published in American Psychologist in 2009, which obtained obedience rates close to Milgram\'s. The empirical phenomenon is settled even as its ethics and interpretation remain debated.',
