        reason: 'The reconstructed royal pedigree — Tutankhamun as the son of Akhenaten (KV55) and a sister-wife (the KV35 "Younger Lady") — became the standard reference for the late 18th-Dynasty family tree and was the first application of genetic fingerprinting to ancient Egyptian royalty. While the specific diagnosis of his cause of death (malaria plus a bone disorder) and some kinship readings have been debated, the core parentage findings from the DNA analysis are widely cited as settled.',
