        reason: 'Ottoman forces invaded Cyprus on 3 July 1570 and, after taking Paphos and Limassol, laid siege to Nicosia. The city held for over a month until 9 September 1570, when the fifteenth assault breached the walls after the defenders had exhausted their ammunition; roughly 20,000 inhabitants were killed in the ensuing massacre. The fall was reported across the Venetian Mediterranean and helped galvanise the formation of the Holy League.',
