        reason: 'King Frederick II granted Tycho Brahe the island of Hven and funds to build an observatory after Tycho\'s 1572 observation of the new star (nova) had made his reputation. The cornerstone of Uraniborg was laid on 8 August 1576, and the sandstone- and limestone-framed brick building was constructed from 1576 to 1580, equipped with large mural quadrants and other instruments for measuring stellar and planetary positions with unprecedented precision.',
