        reason: 'In the July 1948 issue of the Bell System Technical Journal (vol. 27, no. 3, pp. 379–423), Claude Shannon of Bell Telephone Laboratories published the first part of "A Mathematical Theory of Communication," with the second part following in the October 1948 issue (no. 4, pp. 623–656). The paper formalised communication as a statistical problem, defined the "bit" as the unit of information, introduced the entropy measure H = −Σ p log p of an information source, and proved that a noisy channel has a definite capacity below which messages can be transmitted with arbitrarily small error.',
