    text: 'In 1949 Maria Goeppert Mayer and, independently, J. Hans D. Jensen with Otto Haxel and Hans Suess established the nuclear shell model with strong spin-orbit coupling, explaining the "magic numbers" (2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126) of unusually stable nuclei — a result for which Goeppert Mayer and Jensen shared the 1963 Nobel Prize in Physics.',
