        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'Maria Goeppert Mayer, in "On Closed Shells in Nuclei. II" (received February 1949, Physical Review 75:1969, June 1949), showed that adding a strong spin-orbit interaction to the nuclear single-particle potential reproduces exactly the observed magic numbers of nucleon shell closures. Independently, Otto Haxel, J. Hans D. Jensen and Hans Suess reached the same conclusion in "On the \'Magic Numbers\' in Nuclear Structure" (received April 1949, Physical Review 75:1766, June 1949), resolving why nuclei with 2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82 or 126 protons or neutrons are especially stable.',
