    text: 'On 17 August 2018 the International Wheat Genome Sequencing Consortium published in Science the first ordered, fully annotated reference genome of bread wheat (Triticum aestivum) — IWGSC RefSeq v1.0 — representing the roughly 16-gigabase hexaploid genome in 21 pseudomolecules covering about 94% of the genome with 107,891 high-confidence genes, after the large polyploid wheat genome had for years been regarded as too big and complex to assemble.',
