        occurredAt: '2018-08-17',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'On 17 August 2018 Science published "Shifting the limits in wheat research and breeding using a fully annotated reference genome" by the International Wheat Genome Sequencing Consortium, the product of thirteen years of collaborative work. Bread wheat\'s genome is about five times the size of the human genome, hexaploid (three closely related subgenomes A, B and D), and more than 85% repetitive — features that had made an ordered reference seem intractable. RefSeq v1.0 ordered the sequence into 21 chromosome-scale pseudomolecules covering ~94% of the genome and annotated 107,891 high-confidence gene models.',
