    text: 'On 6 April 2006 Edward Daeschler, Neil Shubin and Farish Jenkins published in Nature the description of Tiktaalik roseae, a roughly 375-million-year-old Late Devonian fossil from Ellesmere Island in Arctic Canada that combined fish features (scales, gills, fins) with tetrapod features — a mobile neck, robust limb-like fin bones and a functional wrist — a long-predicted transitional form between lobe-finned fish and the first land vertebrates, and found in rocks of exactly the age the hypothesis predicted.',
