        occurredAt: '2006-04-06',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The team had deliberately searched Devonian freshwater deposits of the right age (≈375 Ma) on Ellesmere Island for a fish-tetrapod intermediate, and in 2004 recovered well-preserved specimens. Their two papers in Nature on 6 April 2006 described Tiktaalik roseae and its anatomy — gills and scales alongside a tetrapod-like wrist, neck and ribcage — recording the discovery of the predicted transitional form in the peer-reviewed literature.',
