        reason: 'A cult had grown around Ulrich\'s tomb at the church of St Afra in Augsburg, with reported miracles and healings after his death in 973. Bishop Liutolf of Augsburg petitioned Rome, and at a synod convened in the Lateran on 31 January 993 Pope John XV pronounced Ulrich a saint. The pope set out the act and the reasons for it in an encyclical bull addressed to the bishops of Gaul and Germany, dated 3 February 993 — the earliest surviving papal canonization document, which transferred the determination of sainthood from local authority to the papacy.',
