        reason: 'Addressing a closed gathering of SS-Gruppenführer in the Posen town hall, Himmler abandoned the usual euphemisms and spoke explicitly of "the extermination of the Jewish people" as a task being carried out, praising those who performed it and stressing that it would remain "a never-to-be-written page of glory" — i.e. deliberately undocumented. He returned to the theme in a second speech to Reichsleiter and Gauleiter on 6 October 1943. The first speech was captured on wax phonograph master plates and as a typed transcript with Himmler\'s handwritten corrections.',
