        reason: 'Warren had observed curved bacteria in stomach biopsies, and Marshall cultured the organism (after an accidental long incubation) and linked it to gastritis and ulcers. Their paper "Unidentified curved bacilli in the stomach of patients with gastritis and peptic ulceration" (The Lancet 323(8390):1311–1315, 16 June 1984) recorded the claim against an entrenched consensus that bacteria could not survive in gastric acid; Marshall later drank a culture and gave himself gastritis to help satisfy Koch\'s postulates.',
