        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'PUBLIC',
        occurredAt: '0537-12-27',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'After the original basilica on the site was burned in the Nika riots of January 532, Justinian commissioned a wholly new church on a vast scale. The geometers Anthemius of Tralles and Isidore of Miletus raised a 31-metre dome on pendentives over a square nave in five years and ten months; the emperor and Patriarch Menas inaugurated it on 27 December 537. The dedication date is fixed in the Byzantine chronicle record — the Chronicon Paschale and the continuation of Marcellinus Comes — and the building itself, described by Procopius in De aedificiis, survives.',
