        reason: 'In his own words preserved in the Hakimi Zij, Ibn Yunus wrote: "This lunar eclipse was on 10 Shawwal 370 H. We gathered to observe this eclipse at al-Qarafa, in the Mosque of Ibn Nasr al-Maghribi" — recording the timing of the eclipse relative to fixed-star altitudes. It is one of several dated solar and lunar eclipses (also 993, 1001, 1002 and 1004) he logged at Cairo under the Fatimid caliph al-Hakim, made with large instruments to a standard of accuracy unmatched in his era.',
