    text: 'In 1693 Edmond Halley published "An Estimate of the Degrees of the Mortality of Mankind" in the Philosophical Transactions, building one of the first true life tables from the birth and death registers of the city of Breslau (Wrocław) supplied by Caspar Neumann — work that put the pricing of life annuities on a mathematical footing and founded actuarial science.',
