        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1845-12-08',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'After the discovery of Vesta in 1807, no further asteroids were found for nearly four decades and many astronomers believed only four such bodies existed. Karl Ludwig Hencke, a postmaster in Driesen searching the sky as an amateur, found a new moving object on 8 December 1845; it was confirmed as the fifth minor planet and named Astraea. The find ended the 38-year drought and prompted a deliberate, systematic search of the zone between Mars and Jupiter.',
