        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Meeting in person for the first time at the Soviet embassy in Tehran from 28 November to 1 December 1943, Roosevelt, Churchill and Stalin agreed the timing of the Western second front and the eastward Soviet offensive that would accompany it. On 1 December 1943 the three leaders issued and signed the Declaration of the Three Powers — "We have concluded our conferences… and we leave here friends in fact, in spirit, and in purpose" — recording their determination to work together in war and peace.',
