    text: 'In 1962 John Gurdon produced cloned frogs by transplanting nuclei from differentiated intestinal epithelial cells of feeding Xenopus tadpoles into enucleated eggs, demonstrating that the nucleus of a specialised adult-type cell retains a complete and functional genome — genomic equivalence — and can be reprogrammed to direct development of an entire organism.',
