    text: 'On 19 March 1965 Robert Holley and colleagues published the complete nucleotide sequence of yeast alanine transfer RNA — 77 nucleotides — the first time the full sequence of any nucleic acid had been determined, and the structure that revealed the cloverleaf folding of tRNA and how the molecule adapts the genetic code to protein synthesis.',
