        reason: 'After roughly seven years isolating gram quantities of pure alanine tRNA from yeast and developing methods to cleave it into overlapping fragments with ribonucleases, Holley\'s group at Cornell reconstructed the order of all 77 nucleotides. They reported it in "Structure of a Ribonucleic Acid" (Science, vol. 147, no. 3664, pp. 1462–1465, 19 March 1965), the first complete primary structure of a nucleic acid and the first to display the cloverleaf secondary structure.',
