        reason: 'After protracted civil litigation (Hampton v. Hanrahan), in November 1982 the survivors and the families of Hampton and Clark received a $1.85 million settlement paid jointly by the federal government, Cook County, and the City of Chicago — a legal resolution that treated the raid as wrongful and cemented the corrected account of a one-sided police assault carried out in the context of the FBI\'s COINTELPRO programme.',
