    text: 'At the close of COP27 in Sharm el-Sheikh on 20 November 2022, governments took the decision to establish a dedicated "loss and damage" fund to help developing countries hit hardest by climate disasters — a demand pressed by vulnerable nations for three decades and long resisted by wealthy states; the fund was operationalised on the opening day of COP28 a year later.',
