    text: 'On 2 July 1937 the aviator Amelia Earhart and her navigator Fred Noonan vanished over the central Pacific near Howland Island during an attempted around-the-world flight; their last radio transmissions were logged by the U.S. Coast Guard cutter Itasca, but neither the aircraft nor their remains have ever been conclusively found, and the fate of the flight remains officially unresolved.',
