        reason: 'Chatterjee and colleagues, using the Very Large Array and very-long-baseline interferometry, pinpointed the repeating burst source FRB 121102 to a persistent radio counterpart in a dwarf star-forming galaxy about three billion light-years distant, in work published in Nature in early January 2017. The precise extragalactic localization settled the long-standing question of whether fast radio bursts were real cosmic events rather than instrumental or local artefacts.',
