    text: 'On 6 February 1886 Clemens Winkler at the Freiberg Mining Academy discovered a new element — germanium — in the mineral argyrodite; its measured properties (atomic mass ≈72.6, grey colour, density ≈5.35, a refractory dioxide) matched almost exactly the "eka-silicon" that Dmitri Mendeleev had predicted from the gaps in his 1871 periodic table, becoming a decisive confirmation of the periodic law.',
