        reason: 'Winkler initially suspected the element fitted Mendeleev\'s predicted "eka-cadmium" or "eka-antimony," but comparison soon showed it was the missing "eka-silicon" Mendeleev had described in 1871: predicted atomic mass 72.64 vs measured 72.63, predicted density 5.5 vs 5.35 g/cm³, both grey, both forming a high-melting dioxide. The near-exact agreement was hailed across the chemical literature — together with gallium (1875) and scandium (1879) — as one of the great empirical vindications of the periodic system, and germanium\'s identity and placement remain settled.',
