        reason: 'After the meridian survey was completed, the definitive platinum standards — the mètre des archives (defined as 443.296 lignes) and the kilogramme des archives — were fabricated and deposited in the French National Archives in June 1799, and the metric system was made the sole legal system of weights and measures in France by the law of 19 frimaire an VIII (10 December 1799). The decimal metre-kilogram framework spread internationally through the 19th century and was placed under permanent international governance by the Metre Convention of 20 May 1875, remaining the foundation of the modern SI.',
