    text: 'Beginning with a spectrogram of the Andromeda Nebula (M31) first obtained on 17 September 1912, Vesto Slipher measured that the nebula is approaching the Sun at roughly 300 km/s — by far the largest radial velocity then known — the first measurement of what would later be recognised as a galaxy\'s Doppler shift and the empirical seed of the expanding-universe picture.',
