        reason: 'Using the Lowell Observatory 24-inch refractor with a fast spectrograph, Slipher exposed his first usable spectrogram of the Andromeda Nebula on 17 September 1912 and, refining the result over the following months, found the nebula\'s spectral lines shifted toward the blue by an amount corresponding to an approach velocity of about 300 km/s — the greatest radial velocity yet observed for any body. He published the result as "The Radial Velocity of the Andromeda Nebula" in Lowell Observatory Bulletin No. 58 (1913).',
