        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1939-02-15',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Building on Richard Tolman\'s general-relativistic equations of stellar structure and on Lev Landau\'s 1938 conjecture of neutron cores in stars, Oppenheimer and Volkoff integrate the equation of hydrostatic equilibrium for a degenerate neutron gas in the Schwarzschild interior metric. They find that solutions reach a maximum mass beyond which the star cannot be supported against gravity and must continue to collapse — the first quantitative upper bound on neutron-star mass. The paper was received by Physical Review on 3 January 1939 and appeared in the issue of 15 February 1939.',
