        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '1231-04-13',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'After the 1229 dispersal, when royal officers killed students and the masters left Paris in protest, Gregory IX intervened on the university\'s side. The bull — dated in its own text "at the Lateran, on the Ides of April, in the fifth year of our pontificate" (13 April 1231) — confirmed the masters\' right to make statutes governing the manner and hours of lectures, dress, funerals, and the cessation of teaching as a corporate weapon, placing the studium under papal protection.',
