    text: 'At the Roman Lenten synod of February 1079, under Pope Gregory VII, Berengar of Tours was compelled to swear an oath confessing that the bread and wine of the altar are "substantially changed" into the true flesh and blood of Christ — an early authoritative affirmation of the eucharistic real presence that anticipated the doctrine of transubstantiation; once back in France, Berengar publicly retracted his recantation.',
