        reason: 'Scott, Edward Wilson and Henry Bowers died in their tent around late March 1912, about 18 km from a supply depot; Edgar Evans and Lawrence Oates had died earlier on the march. On 12 November 1912 a search party found the snow-covered tent containing the three bodies, Scott\'s diaries, letters, and geological specimens. The diaries — published worldwide after the news reached Britain on 10 February 1913 — became the definitive primary record of the expedition\'s fate and of Amundsen\'s priority, and the facts have not since been in dispute.',
