        reason: 'Performing a vivisection on a well-fed dog on 23 July 1622, Aselli noticed white, cord-like vessels filled with a milky fluid spread across the mesentery. Recognising they were not nerves, he identified them as vessels carrying chyle (the "lacteals") and confirmed by repeated dissections that they filled only after the animal had eaten — a structure unknown to Galenic anatomy.',
