        reason: 'Aselli\'s posthumous De lactibus sive lacteis venis (Milan, 1627) — the first scientific work printed with coloured anatomical illustrations — disseminated the discovery. Although Aselli wrongly routed the lacteals toward the liver, the existence of the lacteal/lymphatic vessels was confirmed and extended by Jean Pecquet (thoracic duct and cisterna chyli, 1651) and Thomas Bartholin, definitively overturning Galen\'s claim that the liver formed blood from venous chyle.',
