    text: 'Zhong Zhong and Hua Hua, two long-tailed macaques born in late 2017 at the Institute of Neuroscience of the Chinese Academy of Sciences in Shanghai, were the first primates ever cloned by somatic cell nuclear transfer — the Dolly-the-sheep technique — resolving a two-decade open question about whether the method could work in primates; the result was published in Cell on 24 January 2018.',
