        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '1999-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'After Dolly the sheep was cloned by somatic cell nuclear transfer (SCNT) in 1996, repeated attempts to extend the method to monkeys failed, and by the late 1990s it was widely doubted whether primates — including humans — could be cloned by SCNT at all. Whether a viable primate could be produced from an ordinary body-cell nucleus remained an open scientific question for two decades.',
