        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2018-01-24',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'A team led by Qiang Sun and Mu-ming Poo at the Institute of Neuroscience, Chinese Academy of Sciences in Shanghai, reported in Cell that two healthy macaque infants — Zhong Zhong (born 27 November 2017) and Hua Hua (born 5 December 2017) — had been produced from fetal fibroblast nuclei by SCNT, the first primates cloned by the technique that produced Dolly. The peer-reviewed paper "Cloning of Macaque Monkeys by Somatic Cell Nuclear Transfer" placed the result on the international scientific record.',
