        reason: 'Wang Jun and colleagues at BGI sequenced the genome of an anonymous male Han Chinese individual (designated YH, for "Yanhuang") to 36-fold average coverage using massively parallel Illumina sequencing, identifying about 3.07 million single-nucleotide polymorphisms. Published in Nature, it was the first diploid genome from an East Asian — a population making up nearly 30% of humanity — and the first whole-genome sequence available from a non-European, complementing the earlier Watson and Venter genomes.',
