        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2020-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'For decades the existence of "PeVatrons" — Galactic objects able to accelerate cosmic rays to petaelectronvolt energies — was inferred but unconfirmed, because no instrument had directly detected the predicted PeV-scale gamma rays. Whether and where such accelerators operate in the Milky Way remained an open question in high-energy astrophysics.',
