        toAxis: 'RECORDED',
        community: 'EXPERT_LITERATURE',
        occurredAt: '2021-05-17',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The LHAASO collaboration reported in Nature, in "Ultrahigh-energy photons up to 1.4 petaelectronvolts from 12 γ-ray Galactic sources," the direct detection of photons above 100 TeV — including one near 1.4 PeV — from a dozen sources in the Galactic plane. The result demonstrated that PeVatrons exist and are common in the Milky Way and set a new record for the highest-energy photons observed, placing the discovery on the international scientific record.',
