        reason: 'During the transit of 6 June 1761 (26 May Old Style), Lomonosov noted that as Venus touched the solar limb a faint bright arc appeared around the part of the planet still off the Sun, and that the Sun\'s edge appeared blurred or bulged where Venus entered. He published these observations the same year in "Явление Венеры на Солнце" ("The Appearance of Venus on the Sun"), interpreting the effects as refraction of sunlight by a gaseous envelope and concluding that Venus possesses an atmosphere comparable to or greater than Earth\'s — recording the first claimed detection of a planetary atmosphere beyond Earth.',
