    text: 'In June 1898, working in London, William Ramsay and Morris Travers isolated neon — a new noble-gas element — by fractionally distilling liquefied air and identifying it through the brilliant crimson glow of its spectral discharge, the second of the three noble gases (neon, krypton, xenon) they discovered that year.',
