    text: 'The term "artificial intelligence" was coined in the proposal for the Dartmouth Summer Research Project on Artificial Intelligence, submitted by John McCarthy, Marvin Minsky, Nathaniel Rochester, and Claude Shannon on 2 September 1955; the eight-week workshop they convened at Dartmouth College in the summer of 1956 is generally taken as the founding event of artificial intelligence as a field.',
