        reason: 'On 2 September 1955 McCarthy (then at Dartmouth), Minsky, Rochester (IBM), and Shannon (Bell Labs) formally proposed a summer research project, requesting Rockefeller Foundation support. The proposal is credited with introducing the term "artificial intelligence" and set out the conjecture "that every aspect of learning or any other feature of intelligence can in principle be so precisely described that a machine can be made to simulate it." The named topics included automatic computers, neuron nets, the theory of computation, self-improvement, abstraction, and randomness and creativity.',
