        reason: 'The workshop ran for roughly eight weeks (about 18 June to 17 August 1956) at Dartmouth College, gathering McCarthy, Minsky, Rochester, Shannon, and others including Allen Newell, Herbert Simon, Arthur Samuel, and Ray Solomonoff. Histories of computing and AI consistently treat the 1955 proposal as the origin of the name "artificial intelligence" and the 1956 Dartmouth meeting as the field\'s founding event; the authorship, dates, and naming are settled in the scholarship.',
