        reason: 'FORTRAN was rapidly adopted across scientific and engineering computing and inspired the whole family of high-level languages; it was standardised by the American Standards Association as FORTRAN (ANSI X3.9-1966) in 1966 — the first ever formally standardised programming language — and remains in use, repeatedly revised, into the present. The language\'s priority as the first widely used compiled high-level language and the 1956–57 origin dates are settled in the history of computing.',
