        reason: 'After an on-pad engine shutdown scrubbed the launch on 12 December, Gemini 6A lifted off at 8:37 a.m. EST on 15 December 1965 and, using its onboard radar and thrusters, closed on the already-orbiting Gemini 7 over roughly 270 minutes of close manoeuvring, coming as near as about one foot (30 cm) while the crews talked by radio. Earlier Soviet pairs of Vostok craft had been launched into nearby orbits but had no means to manoeuvre and came no closer than several kilometres; Gemini 6A/7 was the first controlled rendezvous of two crewed spacecraft, tracked in real time by NASA.',
