    text: 'Chinese court astronomers of the Eastern Jin recorded a "guest star" (客星) at the western wall of Zigong (the Purple Palace enclosure, a circumpolar asterism) in the second lunar month of the fourth year of the Taihe reign period (369 CE), visible until it was extinguished in the seventh month — roughly five months — and preserved in the astronomical treatises of the Book of Jin and the Book of Song.',
