        community: 'INSTITUTIONAL',
        occurredAt: '0369-02-01',
        datePrecision: 'MONTH',
        reason: 'The Eastern Jin astronomical office logged a "guest star" at the west wall of Zigong (紫宮, the Purple Palace circumpolar enclosure) in the second month of Taihe 4, recording that it remained until the seventh month — visible for about five months — before being extinguished. The entry survives in the Treatises on Astronomy of the Book of Jin (Jin shu, ch. 13) and the Book of Song (Song shu, ch. 24), compiled from the contemporaneous Jin court records.',
