    text: 'Alfred Russel Wallace published "On the Law which has Regulated the Introduction of New Species" — the "Sarawak Law" paper — in the Annals and Magazine of Natural History in September 1855, arguing that "Every species has come into existence coincident both in space and time with a pre-existing closely allied species," implying that species arise as modified descendants of earlier ones arranged in a branching tree rather than being independently and immutably created.',
