        occurredAt: '1936-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'Studying seismograms of large earthquakes — including the 1929 Murchison earthquake in New Zealand — Lehmann found that P-waves of significant amplitude reached stations such as Sverdlovsk and Irkutsk that should have lain in the core\'s "shadow zone" if the core were uniformly liquid. She explained these arrivals by postulating that the waves reflected off the boundary of a solid inner core, and presented the result in her aptly titled paper "P′".',
