        reason: 'Du Fay set out the two-kinds rule in a paper written in December 1733, printed in volume 38 of the Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society in 1734 and in his memoirs to the Académie Royale des Sciences. He demonstrated that two pieces of cork electrified from glass repelled each other, two electrified from resin repelled each other, but a glass-charged and a resin-charged body attracted — establishing that there are two opposite electrical states, not one.',
