        reason: 'The inverse-square form was confirmed to ever-higher precision by null experiments testing the absence of charge inside a closed conductor — James Clerk Maxwell\'s spherical-shell test, reported in his Treatise on Electricity and Magnetism (1873), bounded any deviation from the exponent 2 to a tiny fraction. Coulomb\'s law became the experimental foundation of electrostatics, the basis of the electrostatic unit of charge, and a settled cornerstone of classical electromagnetism that every later theory had to reproduce.',
