    text: 'Joseph Goldberger, investigating the pellagra epidemic for the U.S. Public Health Service, argued in Public Health Reports on 26 June 1914 that pellagra was caused by a deficient diet rather than by an infectious agent — overturning the prevailing view that it was a communicable disease and pointing toward the dietary cause later identified as niacin (vitamin B3) deficiency.',
