        reason: 'Goldberger noted that pellagra struck inmates, orphans, and asylum patients but spared the staff who lived alongside them and shared their air and water — a pattern impossible for a contagious disease but consistent with a difference in diet (the institutional poor ate a monotonous corn-based diet). In "The Etiology of Pellagra" in Public Health Reports for 26 June 1914 he concluded the disease was dietary in origin, directly contradicting the dominant infectious-agent hypothesis.',
