        occurredAt: '1964-08-31',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'The electroweak program needed a way for gauge bosons to be massive without spoiling gauge symmetry. In a paper received in June and published in Physical Review Letters on 31 August 1964 ("Broken Symmetry and the Mass of Gauge Vector Mesons", PRL 13, 321), Englert and Brout showed that spontaneous breaking of a local gauge symmetry gives the gauge field a mass. Independently, Peter Higgs\'s paper "Broken Symmetries and the Masses of Gauge Bosons" was published in PRL on 19 October 1964 (PRL 13, 508), and uniquely pointed out that the mechanism entails a new massive scalar boson. The prediction entered the physics literature as a recorded but as-yet-unobserved consequence of the theory.',
