        reason: 'Kuru had been described among the Fore but its cause was disputed — variously attributed to heredity or environment. Gajdusek and Gibbs inoculated chimpanzees intracerebrally with brain tissue from kuru victims; after incubation periods of roughly two years the animals developed a kuru-like syndrome. The result was published as "Experimental transmission of a Kuru-like syndrome to chimpanzees" (Gajdusek, Gibbs & Alpers, Nature 209 (5025): 794–796), placing on the scientific record that kuru was caused by a transmissible agent.',
