        reason: 'The Chinese Academy of Sciences launched the Quantum Experiments at Space Scale (QUESS) satellite, nicknamed Micius, from Jiuquan on 16 August 2016 — the first satellite designed for space-based quantum-information experiments. Whether entangled photons could survive transmission from orbit through the atmosphere to widely separated ground stations, preserving their quantum correlations, was an open experimental question that ground-based optical fibre and free-space links (limited to roughly 100 km by photon loss) could not answer.',
