    text: "On 12 February 1941 Reserve Constable Albert Alexander became the first person treated with injected penicillin, by Howard Florey and Ernst Chain's Oxford team — the first demonstration that penicillin could act as a systemic therapeutic agent against bacterial infection in a human; he improved dramatically within a day but relapsed and died on 15 March 1941 after the tiny purified supply ran out.",
