        reason: "Alexander, dying of a disseminated staphylococcal and streptococcal infection, received injected penicillin on 12 February 1941; within 24 hours his temperature fell, his appetite returned and the infection began to heal. Although Fleming had observed penicillin's antibacterial action in 1928, this was the first recorded evidence that it worked as a systemic cure in a human patient. When the team's scant supply was exhausted, Alexander relapsed and died on 15 March 1941.",
