        reason: 'After the X-ray source Cygnus X-1 was pinpointed in 1971 to the star HDE 226868, Louise Webster and Paul Murdin at the Royal Greenwich Observatory and, independently, Charles Thomas Bolton in Toronto announced in 1972 that Doppler analysis of the star\'s spectrum revealed a massive hidden companion whose mass exceeded the limit for a neutron star — suggesting a black hole. The interpretation was novel and disputed: black holes had been theorised but never observationally established.',
