    text: 'The existence of pentaquarks — exotic hadrons composed of five quarks — was allowed by Murray Gell-Mann\'s 1964 quark model; a wave of claimed observations of a light pentaquark (the Θ⁺, ~1540 MeV/c²) in the early 2000s was later refuted as a statistical artefact, and only on 14 July 2015 did the LHCb collaboration at CERN report two genuine pentaquark states (Pc resonances) in the decay of bottom Lambda baryons, establishing the existence of five-quark hadrons.',
