        occurredAt: '2003-01-01',
        datePrecision: 'YEAR',
        reason: 'Beginning in 2003 several experiments — led by the LEPS collaboration in Japan — reported a resonance near 1540 MeV/c² interpreted as the Θ⁺ pentaquark. The claimed signals could not be reliably reproduced, and by the 2008 Review of Particle Physics the evidence was judged so weak that the particles were considered not to exist, leaving the existence of pentaquarks contested.',
