        reason: 'In his 1871 elaboration of the periodic system Mendeleev left deliberate blanks for elements not yet found and predicted their properties from the trends of their table neighbours. For "eka-aluminium" (the element below aluminium) he forecast an atomic weight near 68, a density of about 5.9 g/cm³, a low melting point, and discovery by spectroscopic means — a set of falsifiable predictions recorded years before any matching element was known.',
