        occurredAt: '1953-05-15',
        datePrecision: 'DAY',
        reason: 'Miller built a closed glass apparatus circulating methane, ammonia, hydrogen and boiling water past a continuous electrical discharge standing in for lightning. After a week the water turned reddish and analysis revealed several amino acids that occur in living proteins. His single-author paper "A Production of Amino Acids Under Possible Primitive Earth Conditions" appeared in Science on 15 May 1953, recording the first synthesis of biological monomers from a simulated prebiotic atmosphere.',
