        reason: 'The result was confirmed within weeks by independent experiments (Garwin, Lederman and Weinrich on muon decay) and rapidly accepted as a permanent feature of the weak interaction. The Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences awarded the 1957 Nobel Prize in Physics to Lee and Yang "for their penetrating investigation of the so-called parity laws," presented on 10 December 1957, settling parity violation as established physics.',
